{"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Wf5KrEb6vrkR"},"source":["# Welcome to Colab!"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"1edGr7JPAZyr"},"source":["## Google Colab is available in VS Code!\n","![logo.webp](data:image/webp;base64,)\n","\n","Try the new <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=Google.colab\">Google Colab extension</a> for Visual Studio Code. You can get up and running in just a few clicks:\n","\n","*  In VS Code, open the <strong><em>Extensions</em></strong> view and search for 'Google Colab' to install.\n","*  Open the kernel selector by creating or opening any <code>.ipynb</code> notebook file in your local workspace and either running a cell or clicking the <strong><em>Select kernel</em></strong> button in the top right.\n","*  Click <strong><em>Colab</em></strong> and then select your desired runtime, sign in with your Google Account and you're all set!\n","\n","See more details in our <a href=\"https://developers.googleblog.com/google-colab-is-coming-to-vs-code\">announcement blog here</a>."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Jp6c2c5p22J0"},"source":["## 🎁 Free-of-charge Pro plan for Gemini and Colab for US university students 🎓\n","\n","Get more access to our most accurate model Gemini 3 Pro for advanced coding, complex research and innovative projects, backed by Colab's dedicated high-compute resources for data science and machine learning.\n","\n","Get the Gemini free-of-charge offer at <a href=\"https://gemini.google/students?utm_source=colab&amp;utm_medium=banner&amp;utm_campaign=students_xpa_us-colab-banner\">gemini.google/students</a>.  \n","Get the Colab free-of-charge offer at <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/signup\">colab.research.google.com/signup</a>.  \n","Terms apply."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"C1XfGyQXQK1n"},"source":["## Access popular AI models via Google Colab-AI without an API key\n","All users have access to most popular LLMs via the <code>google-colab-ai</code> Python library, and paid users have access to a wider selection of models. For more details, refer to <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/googlecolab/colabtools/blob/main/notebooks/Getting_started_with_google_colab_ai.ipynb\">getting started with Google Colab AI</a>.\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"JQesyTg7QSU-"},"outputs":[],"source":["from google.colab import ai\n","response = ai.generate_text(\"What is the capital of France?\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"-sdyeRMXPvU_"},"source":["## Explore the Gemini API\n","The Gemini API gives you access to Gemini models created by Google DeepMind. Gemini models are built from the ground up to be multimodal, so you can reason seamlessly across text, images, code and audio.\n","\n","**How to get started**\n","*  Go to <a href=\"https://aistudio.google.com/\">Google AI Studio</a> and log in with your Google Account.\n","*  <a href=\"https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey\">Create an API key</a>.\n","* Use a quickstart for <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/quickstarts/Get_started.ipynb\">Python</a> or call the REST API using <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/quickstarts/rest/Prompting_REST.ipynb\">curl</a>.\n","\n","**Discover Gemini's advanced capabilities**\n","*  Play with Gemini <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/quickstarts/Image-out.ipynb\">multimodal outputs</a>, mixing text and images in an iterative way.\n","*  Discover the <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/quickstarts/Get_started_LiveAPI.ipynb\">multimodal Live API</a> &#40;demo <a href=\"https://aistudio.google.com/live\">here</a>&#41;.\n","*  Learn how to <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/quickstarts/Spatial_understanding.ipynb&quot;\">analyse images and detect items in your pictures</a> using Gemini &#40;bonus, there's a <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/examples/Spatial_understanding_3d.ipynb\">3D version</a> as well!&#41;.\n","*  Unlock the power of the <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/quickstarts/Get_started_thinking.ipynb\">Gemini thinking model</a>, capable of solving complex tasks with its inner thoughts.\n","      \n","**Explore complex use cases**\n","*  Use <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/examples/Search_grounding_for_research_report.ipynb\">Gemini grounding capabilities</a> to create a report on a company based on what the model can find on the Internet.\n","*  Extract <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/examples/Pdf_structured_outputs_on_invoices_and_forms.ipynb\">invoices and form data from PDFs</a> in a structured way.\n","*  Create <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/google-gemini/cookbook/blob/main/examples/Book_illustration.ipynb\">illustrations based on a whole book</a> using Gemini large context window and Imagen.\n","\n","To learn more, take a look at the <a href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/cookbook\">Gemini cookbook</a> or visit the <a href=\"https://ai.google.dev/docs/\">Gemini API documentation</a>.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"Nma_JWh-W-IF"},"source":["Colab now has AI features powered by <a href=\"https://gemini.google.com\">Gemini</a>. The video below provides information on how to use these features, whether you're new to Python or a seasoned veteran.\n","\n","<center>\n","  <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7RXyqFUR98\" target=\"_blank\">\n","  <img alt='Thumbnail for a video showing three AI-powered Google Colab features' src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" height=\"188\" width=\"336\">\n","  </a>\n","</center>"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"5fCEDCU_qrC0"},"source":["<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","  <h2>What is Colab?</h2>\n","</div>\n","\n","Colab, or ‘Colaboratory’, allows you to write and execute Python in your browser, with\n","- Zero configuration required\n","- Access to GPUs free of charge\n","- Easy sharing\n","\n","Whether you're a <strong>student</strong>, a <strong>data scientist</strong> or an <strong>AI researcher</strong>, Colab can make your work easier. Watch <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=inN8seMm7UI\">Introduction to Colab</a> or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rNgswRZ2C1Y\">Colab features you may have missed</a> to learn more or just get started below!"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"GJBs_flRovLc"},"source":["<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","\n","## <strong>Getting started</strong>\n","</div>\n","\n","The document that you are reading is not a static web page, but an interactive environment called a <strong>Colab notebook</strong> that lets you write and execute code.\n","\n","For example, here is a <strong>code cell</strong> with a short Python script that computes a value, stores it in a variable and prints the result:"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":264,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777553628785,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"gJr_9dXGpJ05","outputId":"5cdabcd4-b21d-4a91-a4d0-3c43607f34cd"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["86400"]},"execution_count":4,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["seconds_in_a_day = 24 * 60 * 60\n","seconds_in_a_day"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"2fhs6GZ4qFMx"},"source":["To execute the code in the above cell, select it with a click and then either press the play button to the left of the code, or use the keyboard shortcut 'Command/Ctrl+Enter'. To edit the code, just click the cell and start editing.\n","\n","Variables that you define in one cell can later be used in other cells:"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":7,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777553628795,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"-gE-Ez1qtyIA","outputId":"d050e492-c893-4ca8-8104-1a1b8efcc240"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/plain":["604800"]},"execution_count":5,"metadata":{},"output_type":"execute_result"}],"source":["seconds_in_a_week = 7 * seconds_in_a_day\n","seconds_in_a_week"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"lSrWNr3MuFUS"},"source":["Colab notebooks allow you to combine <strong>executable code</strong> and <strong>rich text</strong> in a single document, along with <strong>images</strong>, <strong>HTML</strong>, <strong>LaTeX</strong> and more. When you create your own Colab notebooks, they are stored in your Google Drive account. You can easily share your Colab notebooks with co-workers or friends, allowing them to comment on your notebooks or even edit them. To find out more, see <a href=\"/notebooks/basic_features_overview.ipynb\">Overview of Colab</a>. To create a new Colab notebook you can use the File menu above, or use the following link: <a href=\"http://colab.research.google.com#create=true\">Create a new Colab notebook</a>.\n","\n","Colab notebooks are Jupyter notebooks that are hosted by Colab. To find out more about the Jupyter project, see <a href=\"https://www.jupyter.org\">jupyter.org</a>."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"UdRyKR44dcNI"},"source":["<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","\n","## Data science\n","</div>\n","\n","With Colab you can harness the full power of popular Python libraries to analyse and visualise data. The code cell below uses <strong>numpy</strong> to generate some random data, and uses <strong>matplotlib</strong> to visualise it. To edit the code, just click the cell and start editing."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"4_kCnsPUqS6o"},"source":["You can import your own data into Colab notebooks from your Google Drive account, including from spreadsheets, as well as from GitHub and many other sources. To find out more about importing data, and how Colab can be used for data science, see the links below under <a href=\"#working-with-data\">Working with data</a>."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":333},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":109,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777553628907,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"C4HZx7Gndbrh","outputId":"c32bab7d-b1fd-4ef4-a55c-14739f94baa6"},"outputs":[{"data":{"text/markdown":"![Sample Visualization](data:image/png;base64,)","text/plain":["<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["import numpy as np\n","import IPython.display as display\n","from matplotlib import pyplot as plt\n","import io\n","import base64\n","\n","ys = 200 + np.random.randn(100)\n","x = [x for x in range(len(ys))]\n","\n","fig = plt.figure(figsize=(4, 3), facecolor='w')\n","plt.plot(x, ys, '-')\n","plt.fill_between(x, ys, 195, where=(ys > 195), facecolor='g', alpha=0.6)\n","plt.title(\"Sample Visualization\", fontsize=10)\n","\n","data = io.BytesIO()\n","plt.savefig(data)\n","image = F\"data:image/png;base64,{base64.b64encode(data.getvalue()).decode()}\"\n","alt = \"Sample Visualization\"\n","display.display(display.Markdown(F\"\"\"![{alt}]({image})\"\"\"))\n","plt.close(fig)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"VYV91hbKwP2J"},"source":["Colab notebooks execute code on Google's cloud servers, meaning that you can leverage the power of Google hardware, including <a href=\"#using-accelerated-hardware\">GPUs and TPUs</a>, regardless of the power of your machine. All you need is a browser.\n","\n","For example, if you find yourself waiting for <strong>pandas</strong> code to finish running and want to go faster, you can switch to a GPU runtime and use libraries like <a href=\"https://rapids.ai/cudf-pandas\">RAPIDS cuDF</a> that provide zero-code-change acceleration."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"vwnNlNIEwoZ8"},"source":["To learn more about accelerating pandas on Colab, see the <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/rapidsai-community/showcase/blob/main/getting_started_tutorials/cudf_pandas_colab_demo.ipynb\">10-minute guide</a> or\n"," <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/rapidsai-community/showcase/blob/main/getting_started_tutorials/cudf_pandas_stocks_demo.ipynb\">US stock market data analysis demo</a>."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"OwuxHmxllTwN"},"source":["<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","\n","## Machine learning\n","</div>\n","\n","With Colab you can import an image dataset, train an image classifier on it and evaluate the model, all in just <a href=\"https://colab.research.google.com/github/tensorflow/docs/blob/master/site/en/tutorials/quickstart/beginner.ipynb\">a few lines of code</a>."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ufxBm1yRnruN"},"source":["Colab is used extensively in the machine learning community with applications including:\n","- Getting started with TensorFlow\n","- Developing and training neural networks\n","- Experimenting with TPUs\n","- Disseminating AI research\n","- Creating tutorials\n","\n","To see sample Colab notebooks that demonstrate machine learning applications, see the <a href=\"#machine-learning-examples\">machine learning examples</a> below."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"-Rh3-Vt9Nev9"},"source":["<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","\n","## More resources\n","\n","### Working with notebooks in Colab\n","\n","</div>\n","\n","- [Overview of Colab](/notebooks/basic_features_overview.ipynb)\n","- [Guide to markdown](/notebooks/markdown_guide.ipynb)\n","- [Importing libraries and installing dependencies](/notebooks/snippets/importing_libraries.ipynb)\n","- [Saving and loading notebooks in GitHub](https://colab.research.google.com/github/googlecolab/colabtools/blob/main/notebooks/colab-github-demo.ipynb)\n","- [Interactive forms](/notebooks/forms.ipynb)\n","- [Interactive widgets](/notebooks/widgets.ipynb)\n","\n","<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","\n","<a name=\"working-with-data\"></a>\n","### Working with data\n","</div>\n","\n","- [Loading data: Drive, Sheets and Google Cloud Storage](/notebooks/io.ipynb)\n","- [Charts: visualising data](/notebooks/charts.ipynb)\n","- [Getting started with BigQuery](/notebooks/bigquery.ipynb)\n","\n","<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","\n","### Machine learning\n","\n","<div>\n","\n","These are a few of the notebooks related to machine learning, including Google's online machine learning course. See the <a href=\"https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/crash-course/\">full course website</a> for more.\n","- [Intro to Pandas DataFrame](https://colab.research.google.com/github/google/eng-edu/blob/main/ml/cc/exercises/pandas_dataframe_ultraquick_tutorial.ipynb)\n","- [Intro to RAPIDS cuDF to accelerate pandas](https://nvda.ws/rapids-cudf)\n","- [Getting started with cuML's accelerator mode](https://colab.research.google.com/github/rapidsai-community/showcase/blob/main/getting_started_tutorials/cuml_sklearn_colab_demo.ipynb)\n","\n","<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","\n","<a name=\"using-accelerated-hardware\"></a>\n","### Using accelerated hardware\n","</div>\n","\n","- [Train a CNN to classify handwritten digits on the MNIST dataset using Flax NNX API](https://colab.research.google.com/github/google/flax/blob/main/docs_nnx/mnist_tutorial.ipynb)\n","- [Train a Vision Transformer &#40;ViT&#41; for image classification with JAX](https://colab.research.google.com/github/jax-ml/jax-ai-stack/blob/main/docs/source/JAX_Vision_transformer.ipynb)\n","- [Text classification with a transformer language model using JAX](https://colab.research.google.com/github/jax-ml/jax-ai-stack/blob/main/docs/source/JAX_transformer_text_classification.ipynb)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"P-H6Lw1vyNNd"},"source":["<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","\n","<a name=\"machine-learning-examples\"></a>\n","\n","### Featured examples\n","\n","</div>\n","\n","- <a href=\"https://docs.jaxstack.ai/en/latest/JAX_for_LLM_pretraining.html\">Train a miniGPT language model with JAX AI stack</a>\n","- <a href=\"https://github.com/google/tunix/blob/main/examples/qlora_gemma.ipynb\">LoRA/QLoRA finetuning for LLM using Tunix</a>\n","- <a href=\"https://keras.io/examples/keras_recipes/parameter_efficient_finetuning_of_gemma_with_lora_and_qlora/\">Parameter-efficient fine-tuning of Gemma with LoRA and QLoRA</a>\n","- <a href=\"https://keras.io/keras_hub/guides/hugging_face_keras_integration/\">Loading Hugging Face transformers checkpoints</a>\n","- <a href=\"https://keras.io/guides/int8_quantization_in_keras/\">8-bit integer quantisation in Keras</a>\n","- <a href=\"https://keras.io/examples/keras_recipes/float8_training_and_inference_with_transformer/\">Float8 training and inference with a simple transformer model</a>\n","- <a href=\"https://keras.io/keras_hub/guides/transformer_pretraining/\">Pretraining a transformer from scratch with KerasHub</a>\n","- <a href=\"https://keras.io/examples/vision/mnist_convnet/\">Simple MNIST convnet</a>\n","- <a href=\"https://keras.io/examples/vision/image_classification_from_scratch/\">Image classification from scratch using Keras 3</a>\n","- <a href=\"https://keras.io/keras_hub/guides/classification_with_keras_hub/\">Image classification with KerasHub</a>\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"2Cw_XUFqRG70"},"outputs":[],"source":[]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":32313,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777553661225,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"UDYGB0kvRKML","outputId":"ce2b8efb-099d-432c-b92b-35689027cd7b"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Mounted at /gdrive\n","/gdrive\n"]}],"source":["from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/gdrive')\n","%cd /gdrive"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"ccJEapEQRNAK"},"outputs":[],"source":[]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":13104,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777553674325,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"vJ6BdRj-RYj8","outputId":"2879ccc7-66d4-4f02-ca34-4b13a688a6cf"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["\u001b[?25l   \u001b[90m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m \u001b[32m0.0/154.8 kB\u001b[0m \u001b[31m?\u001b[0m eta \u001b[36m-:--:--\u001b[0m\r\u001b[2K   \u001b[90m━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\u001b[0m \u001b[32m154.8/154.8 kB\u001b[0m \u001b[31m6.4 MB/s\u001b[0m eta \u001b[36m0:00:00\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[?25hGPU available: True\n","GPU name: Tesla T4\n"]}],"source":["!pip install segmentation-models-pytorch albumentations -q\n","import torch\n","print(\"GPU available:\", torch.cuda.is_available())\n","print(\"GPU name:\", torch.cuda.get_device_name(0) if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"None\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":176},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":25,"status":"error","timestamp":1777553674352,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"0S6NyP_xRhyx","outputId":"1302d36c-ae97-4591-ce60-0b459ec9b68c"},"outputs":[{"ename":"FileNotFoundError","evalue":"[Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/train/src'","output_type":"error","traceback":["\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m","\u001b[0;31mFileNotFoundError\u001b[0m                         Traceback (most recent call last)","\u001b[0;32m/tmp/ipykernel_2292/902672607.py\u001b[0m in \u001b[0;36m<cell line: 0>\u001b[0;34m()\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m      4\u001b[0m     \u001b[0msrc\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m \u001b[0mos\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m.\u001b[0m\u001b[0mpath\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m.\u001b[0m\u001b[0mjoin\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0mdataset_path\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0msplit\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m\"src\"\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m      5\u001b[0m     \u001b[0mgt\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m \u001b[0mos\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m.\u001b[0m\u001b[0mpath\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m.\u001b[0m\u001b[0mjoin\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0mdataset_path\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0msplit\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m\"gt\"\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0;32m----> 6\u001b[0;31m     \u001b[0mprint\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34mf\"{split}: {len(os.listdir(src))} images, {len(os.listdir(gt))} masks\"\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0m","\u001b[0;31mFileNotFoundError\u001b[0m: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/train/src'"]}],"source":["import os\n","dataset_path = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD\"\n","for split in [\"train\", \"val\", \"test\"]:\n","    src = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","    gt  = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","    print(f\"{split}: {len(os.listdir(src))} images, {len(os.listdir(gt))} masks\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"eOcIOVXORq-Z"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","# Search for VDD folder in your Drive\n","base = \"/content/drive/MyDrive\"\n","for item in os.listdir(base):\n","    print(item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"iVw8q3IqRa5w"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","# Search for VDD folder in your Drive\n","base = \"/content/drive/MyDrive\"\n","for item in os.listdir(base):\n","    print(item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"hUf8DHfBRy1x"},"outputs":[],"source":[]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"ASM2kFvvR2cF"},"outputs":[],"source":["from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/content/drive')\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"hEcqkZr3R4xA"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","base = \"/content/drive/MyDrive\"\n","for item in os.listdir(base):\n","    print(item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"sxjRrCJFSBpy"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","vdd_path = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project\"\n","for item in os.listdir(vdd_path):\n","    print(item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"6ybqTE0-SI8p"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","dataset_path = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD\"\n","for split in [\"train\", \"val\", \"test\"]:\n","    src = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","    gt  = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","    print(f\"{split}: {len(os.listdir(src))} images, {len(os.listdir(gt))} masks\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"hIX9a5VYSTXa"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","# Check what's inside VDD_project\n","print(\"Inside VDD_project:\")\n","for item in os.listdir(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project\"):\n","    print(\" \", item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"q6ERaLBBSaJr"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Check what's inside VDD_project/VDD\n","print(\"Inside VDD_project/VDD:\")\n","for item in os.listdir(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD\"):\n","    print(\" \", item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"IIJHKJ1eSeKl"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","print(\"Inside VDD_project/VDD/VD:\")\n","for item in os.listdir(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VD\"):\n","    print(\" \", item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"HoyXCNyFSjCp"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","print(\"Inside VDD_project/VDD/VDD:\")\n","for item in os.listdir(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VD\"):\n","    print(\" \", item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"v8vR4zTpSnca"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","print(\"Inside VDD_project/VDD/VDD:\")\n","for item in os.listdir(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"):\n","    print(\" \", item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"h1HuHCrASriJ"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","dataset_path = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"\n","for split in [\"train\", \"val\", \"test\"]:\n","    src = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","    gt  = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","    print(f\"{split}: {len(os.listdir(src))} images, {len(os.listdir(gt))} masks\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"HuJWnKVTSzww"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os, sys, yaml, numpy as np, torch, torch.nn as nn, cv2, glob\n","from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n","from PIL import Image\n","from tqdm import tqdm\n","import segmentation_models_pytorch as smp\n","\n","# ── Config ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","DATASET_PATH = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"\n","IMAGE_SIZE   = 512\n","BATCH_SIZE   = 4\n","EPOCHS       = 20\n","LR           = 0.0001\n","NUM_CLASSES  = 7\n","CHECKPOINT   = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_clean_best.pth\"\n","\n","# ── Corruptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","def add_fog(image, severity=2):\n","    fog_intensity = [0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.85, 0.95][severity - 1]\n","    fog_layer = np.ones_like(image, dtype=np.float32) * 255\n","    result = image.astype(np.float32) * (1 - fog_intensity) + fog_layer * fog_intensity\n","    return np.clip(result, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_gaussian_noise(image, severity=2):\n","    std = [0.04, 0.06, 0.09, 0.17, 0.26][severity - 1] * 255\n","    noise = np.random.normal(0, std, image.shape).astype(np.float32)\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) + noise, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_blur(image, severity=2):\n","    k = [3, 5, 7, 9, 11][severity - 1]\n","    return cv2.GaussianBlur(image, (k, k), 0)\n","\n","def reduce_brightness(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.45, 0.3, 0.15][severity - 1]\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) * factor, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def reduce_contrast(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2, 0.1][severity - 1]\n","    mean = np.mean(image)\n","    return np.clip((image.astype(np.float32) - mean) * factor + mean, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","CORRUPTIONS = {\n","    \"fog\": add_fog,\n","    \"gaussian_noise\": add_gaussian_noise,\n","    \"blur\": add_blur,\n","    \"brightness\": reduce_brightness,\n","    \"contrast\": reduce_contrast,\n","}\n","\n","# ── Dataset ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","class VDDDataset(Dataset):\n","    def __init__(self, dataset_path, split=\"train\", image_size=512, augmentation=False, corruption=None, severity=2):\n","        self.image_size  = image_size\n","        self.augmentation = augmentation\n","        self.corruption  = corruption\n","        self.severity    = severity\n","        self.image_dir   = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","        self.mask_dir    = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","        self.images      = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(self.image_dir, \"*.JPG\")))\n","        print(f\"[{split}] Found {len(self.images)} images\")\n","\n","    def __len__(self):\n","        return len(self.images)\n","\n","    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n","        img_path  = self.images[idx]\n","        name      = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(img_path))[0]\n","        mask_path = os.path.join(self.mask_dir, name + \".png\")\n","        image = cv2.cvtColor(cv2.imread(img_path), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","        mask  = np.array(Image.open(mask_path))\n","        if self.augmentation:\n","            corruption = np.random.choice(list(CORRUPTIONS.keys()))\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[corruption](image, severity=np.random.randint(1, 4))\n","        if self.corruption:\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[self.corruption](image, self.severity)\n","        image = cv2.resize(image, (self.image_size, self.image_size))\n","        mask  = cv2.resize(mask,  (self.image_size, self.image_size), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST)\n","        mask  = np.clip(mask, 0, 6)\n","        image = torch.from_numpy(image.astype(np.float32) / 255.0).permute(2, 0, 1)\n","        mask  = torch.from_numpy(mask).long()\n","        return image, mask\n","\n","# ── Metric ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","def compute_miou(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds, labels = preds.cpu().numpy(), labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    ious = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        inter = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        union = ((preds == cls) | (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if union > 0:\n","            ious.append(inter / union)\n","    return np.mean(ious) if ious else 0.0\n","\n","# ── Model ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n","print(f\"Using device: {device}\")\n","\n","model = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name    = \"efficientnet-b0\",\n","    encoder_weights = \"imagenet\",\n","    in_channels     = 3,\n","    classes         = NUM_CLASSES,\n",").to(device)\n","\n","optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=LR)\n","criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n","\n","# ── DataLoaders ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","train_dl = DataLoader(VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"train\", IMAGE_SIZE, augmentation=False),\n","                      batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=True,  num_workers=2)\n","val_dl   = DataLoader(VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"val\",   IMAGE_SIZE, augmentation=False),\n","                      batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n","\n","# ── Training Loop ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n","best_miou = 0.0\n","for epoch in range(1, EPOCHS + 1):\n","    model.train()\n","    total_loss = 0\n","    for images, masks in tqdm(train_dl, desc=f\"Epoch {epoch}/{EPOCHS} [Train]\"):\n","        images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","        optimizer.zero_grad()\n","        loss = criterion(model(images), masks)\n","        loss.backward()\n","        optimizer.step()\n","        total_loss += loss.item()\n","\n","    model.eval()\n","    miou_scores = []\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for images, masks in tqdm(val_dl, desc=f\"Epoch {epoch}/{EPOCHS} [Val]\"):\n","            images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","            preds = torch.argmax(model(images), dim=1)\n","            miou_scores.append(compute_miou(preds, masks))\n","\n","    avg_miou = np.mean(miou_scores)\n","    avg_loss = total_loss / len(train_dl)\n","    print(f\"Epoch {epoch} | Loss: {avg_loss:.4f} | Val mIoU: {avg_miou:.4f}\")\n","\n","    if avg_miou > best_miou:\n","        best_miou = avg_miou\n","        torch.save(model.state_dict(), CHECKPOINT)\n","        print(f\"  Saved best model! mIoU: {best_miou:.4f}\")\n","\n","print(f\"\\nTraining complete! Best mIoU: {best_miou:.4f}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"uxBqmTFLTDv0"},"outputs":[],"source":["from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/gdrive')"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"2YWy0sDdUHzp"},"outputs":[],"source":["# Change these two lines:\n","DATASET_PATH = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"\n","CHECKPOINT   = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_clean_best.pth\""]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"NbOjdt8FUY60"},"outputs":[],"source":["from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/gdrive')\n","\n","import os, sys, yaml, numpy as np, torch, torch.nn as nn, cv2, glob\n","from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n","from PIL import Image\n","from tqdm import tqdm\n","import segmentation_models_pytorch as smp\n","\n","# ── Config ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","DATASET_PATH = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"\n","IMAGE_SIZE   = 512\n","BATCH_SIZE   = 4\n","EPOCHS       = 20\n","LR           = 0.0001\n","NUM_CLASSES  = 7\n","CHECKPOINT   = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_clean_best.pth\"\n","\n","# ── Corruptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","def add_fog(image, severity=2):\n","    fog_intensity = [0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.85, 0.95][severity - 1]\n","    fog_layer = np.ones_like(image, dtype=np.float32) * 255\n","    result = image.astype(np.float32) * (1 - fog_intensity) + fog_layer * fog_intensity\n","    return np.clip(result, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_gaussian_noise(image, severity=2):\n","    std = [0.04, 0.06, 0.09, 0.17, 0.26][severity - 1] * 255\n","    noise = np.random.normal(0, std, image.shape).astype(np.float32)\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) + noise, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_blur(image, severity=2):\n","    k = [3, 5, 7, 9, 11][severity - 1]\n","    return cv2.GaussianBlur(image, (k, k), 0)\n","\n","def reduce_brightness(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.45, 0.3, 0.15][severity - 1]\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) * factor, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def reduce_contrast(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2, 0.1][severity - 1]\n","    mean = np.mean(image)\n","    return np.clip((image.astype(np.float32) - mean) * factor + mean, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","CORRUPTIONS = {\n","    \"fog\": add_fog,\n","    \"gaussian_noise\": add_gaussian_noise,\n","    \"blur\": add_blur,\n","    \"brightness\": reduce_brightness,\n","    \"contrast\": reduce_contrast,\n","}\n","\n","# ── Dataset ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","class VDDDataset(Dataset):\n","    def __init__(self, dataset_path, split=\"train\", image_size=512, augmentation=False, corruption=None, severity=2):\n","        self.image_size   = image_size\n","        self.augmentation = augmentation\n","        self.corruption   = corruption\n","        self.severity     = severity\n","        self.image_dir    = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","        self.mask_dir     = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","        self.images       = sorted(\n","            glob.glob(os.path.join(self.image_dir, \"*.JPG\")) +\n","            glob.glob(os.path.join(self.image_dir, \"*.jpg\"))\n","        )\n","        print(f\"[{split}] Found {len(self.images)} images\")\n","\n","    def __len__(self):\n","        return len(self.images)\n","\n","    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n","        img_path  = self.images[idx]\n","        name      = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(img_path))[0]\n","        mask_path = os.path.join(self.mask_dir, name + \".png\")\n","        image = cv2.cvtColor(cv2.imread(img_path), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","        mask  = np.array(Image.open(mask_path))\n","        if self.augmentation:\n","            corruption = np.random.choice(list(CORRUPTIONS.keys()))\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[corruption](image, severity=np.random.randint(1, 4))\n","        if self.corruption:\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[self.corruption](image, self.severity)\n","        image = cv2.resize(image, (self.image_size, self.image_size))\n","        mask  = cv2.resize(mask,  (self.image_size, self.image_size), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST)\n","        mask  = np.clip(mask, 0, 6)\n","        image = torch.from_numpy(image.astype(np.float32) / 255.0).permute(2, 0, 1)\n","        mask  = torch.from_numpy(mask).long()\n","        return image, mask\n","\n","# ── Metric ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","def compute_miou(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds, labels = preds.cpu().numpy(), labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    ious = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        inter = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        union = ((preds == cls) | (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if union > 0:\n","            ious.append(inter / union)\n","    return np.mean(ious) if ious else 0.0\n","\n","# ── Model ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n","print(f\"Using device: {device}\")\n","\n","model = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name    = \"efficientnet-b0\",\n","    encoder_weights = \"imagenet\",\n","    in_channels     = 3,\n","    classes         = NUM_CLASSES,\n",").to(device)\n","\n","optimizer = torch.optim.Adam(model.parameters(), lr=LR)\n","scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=EPOCHS)\n","criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n","\n","# ── DataLoaders ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","train_dl = DataLoader(VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"train\", IMAGE_SIZE, augmentation=True),\n","                      batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=True,  num_workers=2)\n","val_dl   = DataLoader(VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"val\",   IMAGE_SIZE, augmentation=False),\n","                      batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n","\n","# ── Training Loop ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n","best_miou = 0.0\n","for epoch in range(1, EPOCHS + 1):\n","    model.train()\n","    total_loss = 0\n","    for images, masks in tqdm(train_dl, desc=f\"Epoch {epoch}/{EPOCHS} [Train]\"):\n","        images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","        optimizer.zero_grad()\n","        loss = criterion(model(images), masks)\n","        loss.backward()\n","        optimizer.step()\n","        total_loss += loss.item()\n","\n","    model.eval()\n","    miou_scores = []\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for images, masks in tqdm(val_dl, desc=f\"Epoch {epoch}/{EPOCHS} [Val]\"):\n","            images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","            preds = torch.argmax(model(images), dim=1)\n","            miou_scores.append(compute_miou(preds, masks))\n","\n","    avg_miou = np.mean(miou_scores)\n","    avg_loss = total_loss / len(train_dl)\n","    print(f\"Epoch {epoch} | Loss: {avg_loss:.4f} | Val mIoU: {avg_miou:.4f}\")\n","    scheduler.step()\n","\n","    if avg_miou > best_miou:\n","        best_miou = avg_miou\n","        torch.save(model.state_dict(), CHECKPOINT)\n","        print(f\"  Saved best model! mIoU: {best_miou:.4f}\")\n","\n","print(f\"\\nTraining complete! Best mIoU: {best_miou:.4f}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"h7934ohFUufk"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","CHECKPOINT = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_clean_best.pth\"\n","if os.path.exists(CHECKPOINT):\n","    print(\"Checkpoint found! Size:\", os.path.getsize(CHECKPOINT) / 1024 / 1024, \"MB\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"No checkpoint found!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"3HS7gGGvOJFK"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","print(\"Inside VDD_project:\")\n","for item in os.listdir(\"/content/drive/MyDrive/VDD_project\"):\n","    print(\" \", item)\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"Piy91ivQOP75"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","print(\"Inside MyDrive:\")\n","for item in os.listdir(\"/gdrive/MyDrive\"):\n","    print(\" \", item)\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"G80OrBYkOWZt"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os\n","\n","print(\"Inside VDD_project:\")\n","for item in os.listdir(\"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project\"):\n","    print(\" \", item)"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"1ywf20WyOgPN"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os, numpy as np, torch, torch.nn as nn, cv2, glob\n","from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n","from PIL import Image\n","from tqdm import tqdm\n","import segmentation_models_pytorch as smp\n","\n","# ── Config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","DATASET_PATH = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"\n","IMAGE_SIZE   = 512\n","BATCH_SIZE   = 4\n","NUM_CLASSES  = 7\n","CHECKPOINT   = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_clean_best.pth\"\n","\n","# ── Corruptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","def add_fog(image, severity=2):\n","    fog_intensity = [0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.85, 0.95][severity - 1]\n","    fog_layer = np.ones_like(image, dtype=np.float32) * 255\n","    result = image.astype(np.float32) * (1 - fog_intensity) + fog_layer * fog_intensity\n","    return np.clip(result, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_gaussian_noise(image, severity=2):\n","    std = [0.04, 0.06, 0.09, 0.17, 0.26][severity - 1] * 255\n","    noise = np.random.normal(0, std, image.shape).astype(np.float32)\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) + noise, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_blur(image, severity=2):\n","    k = [3, 5, 7, 9, 11][severity - 1]\n","    return cv2.GaussianBlur(image, (k, k), 0)\n","\n","def reduce_brightness(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.45, 0.3, 0.15][severity - 1]\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) * factor, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def reduce_contrast(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2, 0.1][severity - 1]\n","    mean = np.mean(image)\n","    return np.clip((image.astype(np.float32) - mean) * factor + mean, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","CORRUPTIONS = {\n","    \"fog\": add_fog,\n","    \"gaussian_noise\": add_gaussian_noise,\n","    \"blur\": add_blur,\n","    \"brightness\": reduce_brightness,\n","    \"contrast\": reduce_contrast,\n","}\n","\n","# ── Dataset ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","class VDDDataset(Dataset):\n","    def __init__(self, dataset_path, split=\"test\", image_size=512, corruption=None, severity=2):\n","        self.image_size = image_size\n","        self.corruption = corruption\n","        self.severity   = severity\n","        self.image_dir  = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","        self.mask_dir   = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","        self.images     = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(self.image_dir, \"*.JP"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"d9f74xOLOou_"},"outputs":[],"source":["import os, numpy as np, torch, torch.nn as nn, cv2, glob\n","from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n","from PIL import Image\n","from tqdm import tqdm\n","import segmentation_models_pytorch as smp\n","\n","DATASET_PATH = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"\n","IMAGE_SIZE   = 512\n","BATCH_SIZE   = 4\n","NUM_CLASSES  = 7\n","CHECKPOINT   = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_clean_best.pth\"\n","print(\"Libraries loaded!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"4dnju0JzOzkL"},"outputs":[],"source":["def add_fog(image, severity=2):\n","    fog_intensity = [0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.85, 0.95][severity - 1]\n","    fog_layer = np.ones_like(image, dtype=np.float32) * 255\n","    result = image.astype(np.float32) * (1 - fog_intensity) + fog_layer * fog_intensity\n","    return np.clip(result, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_gaussian_noise(image, severity=2):\n","    std = [0.04, 0.06, 0.09, 0.17, 0.26][severity - 1] * 255\n","    noise = np.random.normal(0, std, image.shape).astype(np.float32)\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) + noise, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_blur(image, severity=2):\n","    k = [3, 5, 7, 9, 11][severity - 1]\n","    return cv2.GaussianBlur(image, (k, k), 0)\n","\n","def reduce_brightness(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.45, 0.3, 0.15][severity - 1]\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) * factor, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def reduce_contrast(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2, 0.1][severity - 1]\n","    mean = np.mean(image)\n","    return np.clip((image.astype(np.float32) - mean) * factor + mean, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","CORRUPTIONS = {\n","    \"fog\": add_fog,\n","    \"gaussian_noise\": add_gaussian_noise,\n","    \"blur\": add_blur,\n","    \"brightness\": reduce_brightness,\n","    \"contrast\": reduce_contrast,\n","}\n","print(\"Corruptions defined!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"gpSNvggcO4Fs"},"outputs":[],"source":["class VDDDataset(Dataset):\n","    def __init__(self, dataset_path, split=\"test\", image_size=512, corruption=None, severity=2):\n","        self.image_size = image_size\n","        self.corruption = corruption\n","        self.severity   = severity\n","        self.image_dir  = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","        self.mask_dir   = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","        self.images     = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(self.image_dir, \"*.JPG\")))\n","        print(f\"[{split}] Found {len(self.images)} images | Corruption: {corruption or 'None'}\")\n","\n","    def __len__(self):\n","        return len(self.images)\n","\n","    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n","        img_path  = self.images[idx]\n","        name      = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(img_path))[0]\n","        mask_path = os.path.join(self.mask_dir, name + \".png\")\n","        image = cv2.cvtColor(cv2.imread(img_path), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","        mask  = np.array(Image.open(mask_path))\n","        if self.corruption:\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[self.corruption](image, self.severity)\n","        image = cv2.resize(image, (self.image_size, self.image_size))\n","        mask  = cv2.resize(mask, (self.image_size, self.image_size), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST)\n","        mask  = np.clip(mask, 0, 6)\n","        image = torch.from_numpy(image.astype(np.float32) / 255.0).permute(2, 0, 1)\n","        mask  = torch.from_numpy(mask).long()\n","        return image, mask\n","\n","print(\"Dataset class defined!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"oo4YoSFJO740"},"outputs":[],"source":["def compute_miou(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds, labels = preds.cpu().numpy(), labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    ious = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        inter = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        union = ((preds == cls) | (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if union > 0:\n","            ious.append(inter / union)\n","    return np.mean(ious) if ious else 0.0\n","\n","device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n","print(f\"Using device: {device}\")\n","\n","model = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name    = \"efficientnet-b0\",\n","    encoder_weights = None,\n","    in_channels     = 3,\n","    classes         = NUM_CLASSES,\n",").to(device)\n","\n","model.load_state_dict(torch.load(CHECKPOINT, map_location=device))\n","model.eval()\n","print(\"Checkpoint loaded successfully!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"8bdr9H3dO-qo"},"outputs":[],"source":["def evaluate(corruption=None):\n","    ds = VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"test\", IMAGE_SIZE, corruption=corruption)\n","    dl = DataLoader(ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n","    scores = []\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for images, masks in tqdm(dl, desc=f\"Testing [{corruption or 'clean'}]\"):\n","            images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","            preds = torch.argmax(model(images), dim=1)\n","            scores.append(compute_miou(preds, masks))\n","    return np.mean(scores)\n","\n","results = {}\n","results[\"clean\"] = evaluate(corruption=None)\n","print(f\"Clean mIoU: {results['clean']:.4f}\")\n","\n","for corruption in CORRUPTIONS.keys():\n","    results[corruption] = evaluate(corruption=corruption)\n","    gap = results[\"clean\"] - results[corruption]\n","    print(f\"{corruption:20s} mIoU: {results[corruption]:.4f} | Gap: {gap:.4f}\")\n","\n","print(f\"\\n{'='*45}\")\n","print(f\"{'Corruption':<20} {'mIoU':>8} {'Gap':>8}\")\n","print(\"-\" * 45)\n","for k, v in results.items():\n","    gap = results[\"clean\"] - v if k != \"clean\" else 0.0\n","    print(f\"{k:<20} {v:>8.4f} {gap:>8.4f}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":211},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":74,"status":"error","timestamp":1777553699548,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"XBqcBWgdPJIu","outputId":"b0884f83-b8cc-4a76-9115-de426e690025"},"outputs":[{"ename":"NameError","evalue":"name 'Dataset' is not defined","output_type":"error","traceback":["\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m","\u001b[0;31mNameError\u001b[0m                                 Traceback (most recent call last)","\u001b[0;32m/tmp/ipykernel_2292/1508303984.py\u001b[0m in \u001b[0;36m<cell line: 0>\u001b[0;34m()\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m      5\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m      6\u001b[0m \u001b[0;31m# ── Dataset with Augmentation ───────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0;32m----> 7\u001b[0;31m \u001b[0;32mclass\u001b[0m \u001b[0mVDDDatasetAug\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0mDataset\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m:\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m      8\u001b[0m     \u001b[0;32mdef\u001b[0m \u001b[0m__init__\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0mself\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0mdataset_path\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0msplit\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\"train\"\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0mimage_size\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m\u001b[0;36m512\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m,\u001b[0m \u001b[0maugmentation\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m\u001b[0;32mFalse\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m:\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m      9\u001b[0m         \u001b[0mself\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m.\u001b[0m\u001b[0mimage_size\u001b[0m   \u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m \u001b[0mimage_size\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0;31mNameError\u001b[0m: name 'Dataset' is not defined"]}],"source":["# ── Config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","CHECKPOINT_AUG = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_augmented_best.pth\"\n","EPOCHS = 20\n","LR     = 0.0001\n","\n","# ── Dataset with Augmentation ───────────────────────────────────\n","class VDDDatasetAug(Dataset):\n","    def __init__(self, dataset_path, split=\"train\", image_size=512, augmentation=False):\n","        self.image_size   = image_size\n","        self.augmentation = augmentation\n","        self.image_dir    = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","        self.mask_dir     = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","        self.images       = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(self.image_dir, \"*.JPG\")))\n","        print(f\"[{split}] Found {len(self.images)} images | Augmentation: {augmentation}\")\n","\n","    def __len__(self):\n","        return len(self.images)\n","\n","    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n","        img_path  = self.images[idx]\n","        name      = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(img_path))[0]\n","        mask_path = os.path.join(self.mask_dir, name + \".png\")\n","        image = cv2.cvtColor(cv2.imread(img_path), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","        mask  = np.array(Image.open(mask_path))\n","        if self.augmentation:\n","            corruption = np.random.choice(list(CORRUPTIONS.keys()))\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[corruption](image, severity=np.random.randint(1, 4))\n","        image = cv2.resize(image, (self.image_size, self.image_size))\n","        mask  = cv2.resize(mask, (self.image_size, self.image_size), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST)\n","        mask  = np.clip(mask, 0, 6)\n","        image = torch.from_numpy(image.astype(np.float32) / 255.0).permute(2, 0, 1)\n","        mask  = torch.from_numpy(mask).long()\n","        return image, mask\n","\n","# ── New Model ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","model_aug = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name    = \"efficientnet-b0\",\n","    encoder_weights = \"imagenet\",\n","    in_channels     = 3,\n","    classes         = NUM_CLASSES,\n",").to(device)\n","\n","optimizer_aug = torch.optim.Adam(model_aug.parameters(), lr=LR)\n","criterion     = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n","\n","train_dl_aug = DataLoader(VDDDatasetAug(DATASET_PATH, \"train\", IMAGE_SIZE, augmentation=True),\n","                          batch_size=4, shuffle=True, num_workers=2)\n","val_dl_aug   = DataLoader(VDDDatasetAug(DATASET_PATH, \"val\", IMAGE_SIZE, augmentation=False),\n","                          batch_size=4, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n","\n","# ── Training Loop ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n","best_miou_aug = 0.0\n","for epoch in range(1, EPOCHS + 1):\n","    model_aug.train()\n","    total_loss = 0\n","    for images, masks in tqdm(train_dl_aug, desc=f\"Epoch {epoch}/{EPOCHS} [Train]\"):\n","        images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","        optimizer_aug.zero_grad()\n","        loss = criterion(model_aug(images), masks)\n","        loss.backward()\n","        optimizer_aug.step()\n","        total_loss += loss.item()\n","\n","    model_aug.eval()\n","    miou_scores = []\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for images, masks in tqdm(val_dl_aug, desc=f\"Epoch {epoch}/{EPOCHS} [Val]\"):\n","            images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","            preds = torch.argmax(model_aug(images), dim=1)\n","            miou_scores.append(compute_miou(preds, masks))\n","\n","    avg_miou = np.mean(miou_scores)\n","    avg_loss = total_loss / len(train_dl_aug)\n","    print(f\"Epoch {epoch} | Loss: {avg_loss:.4f} | Val mIoU: {avg_miou:.4f}\")\n","\n","    if avg_miou > best_miou_aug:\n","        best_miou_aug = avg_miou\n","        torch.save(model_aug.state_dict(), CHECKPOINT_AUG)\n","        print(f\"  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: {best_miou_aug:.4f}\")\n","\n","print(f\"\\nAugmented Training Complete! Best mIoU: {best_miou_aug:.4f}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":13691,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777553812111,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"R0QfQZsdRRyN","outputId":"3ebdd4a0-f4fd-4815-e40e-b550c80586b4"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Using device: cuda\n","Drive already mounted at /gdrive; to attempt to forcibly remount, call drive.mount(\"/gdrive\", force_remount=True).\n","All setup complete!\n"]}],"source":["# ── Setup Everything ────────────────────────────────────────────\n","import os, numpy as np, torch, torch.nn as nn, cv2, glob\n","from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n","from PIL import Image\n","from tqdm import tqdm\n","import segmentation_models_pytorch as smp\n","\n","DATASET_PATH   = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"\n","IMAGE_SIZE     = 512\n","BATCH_SIZE     = 4\n","NUM_CLASSES    = 7\n","CHECKPOINT     = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_clean_best.pth\"\n","CHECKPOINT_AUG = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_augmented_best.pth\"\n","EPOCHS         = 20\n","LR             = 0.0001\n","\n","# ── Corruptions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","def add_fog(image, severity=2):\n","    fog_intensity = [0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.85, 0.95][severity - 1]\n","    fog_layer = np.ones_like(image, dtype=np.float32) * 255\n","    result = image.astype(np.float32) * (1 - fog_intensity) + fog_layer * fog_intensity\n","    return np.clip(result, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_gaussian_noise(image, severity=2):\n","    std = [0.04, 0.06, 0.09, 0.17, 0.26][severity - 1] * 255\n","    noise = np.random.normal(0, std, image.shape).astype(np.float32)\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) + noise, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_blur(image, severity=2):\n","    k = [3, 5, 7, 9, 11][severity - 1]\n","    return cv2.GaussianBlur(image, (k, k), 0)\n","\n","def reduce_brightness(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.45, 0.3, 0.15][severity - 1]\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) * factor, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def reduce_contrast(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2, 0.1][severity - 1]\n","    mean = np.mean(image)\n","    return np.clip((image.astype(np.float32) - mean) * factor + mean, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","CORRUPTIONS = {\n","    \"fog\": add_fog,\n","    \"gaussian_noise\": add_gaussian_noise,\n","    \"blur\": add_blur,\n","    \"brightness\": reduce_brightness,\n","    \"contrast\": reduce_contrast,\n","}\n","\n","# ── Dataset ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","class VDDDataset(Dataset):\n","    def __init__(self, dataset_path, split=\"test\", image_size=512, augmentation=False, corruption=None, severity=2):\n","        self.image_size   = image_size\n","        self.augmentation = augmentation\n","        self.corruption   = corruption\n","        self.severity     = severity\n","        self.image_dir    = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","        self.mask_dir     = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","        self.images       = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(self.image_dir, \"*.JPG\")))\n","        print(f\"[{split}] Found {len(self.images)} images | Augmentation: {augmentation} | Corruption: {corruption or 'None'}\")\n","\n","    def __len__(self):\n","        return len(self.images)\n","\n","    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n","        img_path  = self.images[idx]\n","        name      = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(img_path))[0]\n","        mask_path = os.path.join(self.mask_dir, name + \".png\")\n","        image = cv2.cvtColor(cv2.imread(img_path), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","        mask  = np.array(Image.open(mask_path))\n","        if self.augmentation:\n","            corruption = np.random.choice(list(CORRUPTIONS.keys()))\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[corruption](image, severity=np.random.randint(1, 4))\n","        if self.corruption:\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[self.corruption](image, self.severity)\n","        image = cv2.resize(image, (self.image_size, self.image_size))\n","        mask  = cv2.resize(mask, (self.image_size, self.image_size), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST)\n","        mask  = np.clip(mask, 0, 6)\n","        image = torch.from_numpy(image.astype(np.float32) / 255.0).permute(2, 0, 1)\n","        mask  = torch.from_numpy(mask).long()\n","        return image, mask\n","\n","# ── Metric ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","def compute_miou(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds, labels = preds.cpu().numpy(), labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    ious = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        inter = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        union = ((preds == cls) | (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if union > 0:\n","            ious.append(inter / union)\n","    return np.mean(ious) if ious else 0.0\n","\n","# ── Device ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n","print(f\"Using device: {device}\")\n","\n","# ── Mount Drive ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/gdrive')\n","print(\"All setup complete!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000,"referenced_widgets":["f3960b22b8cd4692814e4a47a055f33e","645544a48b944a1c86c8a9b28a8215af","88169d52ad4541e0bce2dc9824da91cc","05dedf234964489c95803d266552e403","8ddef393257a455793751401dcd30020","82ba91636a024823bd2769901f4d3ac9","51ea8b31759648858f98d2140c211166","4fa7a505e58b431180bbf691aada91fc","97775b6524c048ccba5a6ed67afe386c","5943af1bd04d4831ae84925b2d4c8757","ab2c8aed6d8541c889e98cf479d56884","4560bf84448c4e7fb8d930dc6eeab6f4","d0592a23c9cc47ad94cc738b6c86b08c","0bf3341c718b40d78a68497eb4f4d638","3275f155b2954f44b7e47f3b5d286c7a","1210910bf7514b9799feedc1e661771a","368edbd8043e45e7b30a592cf6dc5744","03178b334d724091bac7de047b9237f5","1f4fe6b23d824dac99f0de178d5a3a30","1c9d350988f64719a1b7e08fbb00f006","3e68b4dd18514c9ab235347111fa6ba3","7552de59eaa94087b1a6e636bffb31a3"]},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":3670045,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777557551557,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"Q5dGTFSDdnKs","outputId":"37638a0f-128c-42c2-8d38-2dd2aee786fb"},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["/usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/huggingface_hub/utils/_auth.py:93: UserWarning: \n","The secret `HF_TOKEN` does not exist in your Colab secrets.\n","To authenticate with the Hugging Face Hub, create a token in your settings tab (https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens), set it as secret in your Google Colab and restart your session.\n","You will be able to reuse this secret in all of your notebooks.\n","Please note that authentication is recommended but still optional to access public models or datasets.\n","  warnings.warn(\n","Warning: You are sending unauthenticated requests to the HF Hub. Please set a HF_TOKEN to enable higher rate limits and faster downloads.\n","WARNING:huggingface_hub.utils._http:Warning: You are sending unauthenticated requests to the HF Hub. Please set a HF_TOKEN to enable higher rate limits and faster downloads.\n"]},{"data":{"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"model_id":"f3960b22b8cd4692814e4a47a055f33e","version_major":2,"version_minor":0},"text/plain":["config.json:   0%|          | 0.00/106 [00:00<?, ?B/s]"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"model_id":"4560bf84448c4e7fb8d930dc6eeab6f4","version_major":2,"version_minor":0},"text/plain":["model.safetensors:   0%|          | 0.00/21.4M [00:00<?, ?B/s]"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[train] Found 280 images | Augmentation: True | Corruption: None\n","[val] Found 80 images | Augmentation: False | Corruption: None\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 1/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [04:57<00:00,  4.25s/it]\n","Epoch 1/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [01:46<00:00,  5.33s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 1 | Loss: 1.4931 | Val mIoU: 0.2432\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.2432\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 2/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:42<00:00,  2.33s/it]\n","Epoch 2/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.27it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 2 | Loss: 1.0111 | Val mIoU: 0.2720\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.2720\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 3/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:29<00:00,  2.13s/it]\n","Epoch 3/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:16<00:00,  1.21it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 3 | Loss: 0.8589 | Val mIoU: 0.3348\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.3348\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 4/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:20<00:00,  2.01s/it]\n","Epoch 4/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:16<00:00,  1.21it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 4 | Loss: 0.7312 | Val mIoU: 0.3865\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.3865\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 5/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:39<00:00,  2.28s/it]\n","Epoch 5/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.27it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 5 | Loss: 0.6946 | Val mIoU: 0.4113\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.4113\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 6/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:32<00:00,  2.18s/it]\n","Epoch 6/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:17<00:00,  1.17it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 6 | Loss: 0.6190 | Val mIoU: 0.4123\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.4123\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 7/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:36<00:00,  2.23s/it]\n","Epoch 7/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:16<00:00,  1.25it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 7 | Loss: 0.5940 | Val mIoU: 0.4514\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.4514\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 8/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:32<00:00,  2.18s/it]\n","Epoch 8/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.29it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 8 | Loss: 0.5763 | Val mIoU: 0.4259\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 9/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:41<00:00,  2.31s/it]\n","Epoch 9/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.28it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 9 | Loss: 0.5164 | Val mIoU: 0.4534\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.4534\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 10/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:37<00:00,  2.25s/it]\n","Epoch 10/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.26it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 10 | Loss: 0.4740 | Val mIoU: 0.4742\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.4742\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 11/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:38<00:00,  2.27s/it]\n","Epoch 11/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.27it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 11 | Loss: 0.4925 | Val mIoU: 0.4713\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 12/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:26<00:00,  2.09s/it]\n","Epoch 12/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.30it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 12 | Loss: 0.4577 | Val mIoU: 0.4789\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.4789\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 13/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:32<00:00,  2.17s/it]\n","Epoch 13/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.28it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 13 | Loss: 0.4287 | Val mIoU: 0.4951\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.4951\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 14/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:29<00:00,  2.13s/it]\n","Epoch 14/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:16<00:00,  1.24it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 14 | Loss: 0.4387 | Val mIoU: 0.4886\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 15/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:25<00:00,  2.08s/it]\n","Epoch 15/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.28it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 15 | Loss: 0.3943 | Val mIoU: 0.5063\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.5063\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 16/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:33<00:00,  2.20s/it]\n","Epoch 16/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:15<00:00,  1.28it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 16 | Loss: 0.3944 | Val mIoU: 0.5114\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.5114\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 17/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:52<00:00,  2.46s/it]\n","Epoch 17/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:18<00:00,  1.10it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 17 | Loss: 0.3731 | Val mIoU: 0.5180\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.5180\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 18/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:43<00:00,  2.33s/it]\n","Epoch 18/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:17<00:00,  1.16it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 18 | Loss: 0.3965 | Val mIoU: 0.5192\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.5192\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 19/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:44<00:00,  2.35s/it]\n","Epoch 19/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:16<00:00,  1.24it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 19 | Loss: 0.3592 | Val mIoU: 0.5219\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.5219\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 20/20 [Train]: 100%|██████████| 70/70 [02:27<00:00,  2.11s/it]\n","Epoch 20/20 [Val]: 100%|██████████| 20/20 [00:17<00:00,  1.14it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Epoch 20 | Loss: 0.3540 | Val mIoU: 0.5222\n","  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: 0.5222\n","\n","Augmented Training Complete! Best mIoU: 0.5222\n"]}],"source":["# ── Augmented Training ──────────────────────────────────────────\n","model_aug = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name    = \"efficientnet-b0\",\n","    encoder_weights = \"imagenet\",\n","    in_channels     = 3,\n","    classes         = NUM_CLASSES,\n",").to(device)\n","\n","optimizer_aug = torch.optim.Adam(model_aug.parameters(), lr=LR)\n","criterion     = nn.CrossEntropyLoss()\n","\n","train_dl_aug = DataLoader(VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"train\", IMAGE_SIZE, augmentation=True),\n","                          batch_size=4, shuffle=True, num_workers=2)\n","val_dl_aug   = DataLoader(VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"val\", IMAGE_SIZE, augmentation=False),\n","                          batch_size=4, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n","\n","best_miou_aug = 0.0\n","for epoch in range(1, EPOCHS + 1):\n","    model_aug.train()\n","    total_loss = 0\n","    for images, masks in tqdm(train_dl_aug, desc=f\"Epoch {epoch}/{EPOCHS} [Train]\"):\n","        images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","        optimizer_aug.zero_grad()\n","        loss = criterion(model_aug(images), masks)\n","        loss.backward()\n","        optimizer_aug.step()\n","        total_loss += loss.item()\n","\n","    model_aug.eval()\n","    miou_scores = []\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for images, masks in tqdm(val_dl_aug, desc=f\"Epoch {epoch}/{EPOCHS} [Val]\"):\n","            images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","            preds = torch.argmax(model_aug(images), dim=1)\n","            miou_scores.append(compute_miou(preds, masks))\n","\n","    avg_miou = np.mean(miou_scores)\n","    avg_loss = total_loss / len(train_dl_aug)\n","    print(f\"Epoch {epoch} | Loss: {avg_loss:.4f} | Val mIoU: {avg_miou:.4f}\")\n","\n","    if avg_miou > best_miou_aug:\n","        best_miou_aug = avg_miou\n","        torch.save(model_aug.state_dict(), CHECKPOINT_AUG)\n","        print(f\"  Saved best augmented model! mIoU: {best_miou_aug:.4f}\")\n","\n","print(f\"\\nAugmented Training Complete! Best mIoU: {best_miou_aug:.4f}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":219258,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777557859530,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"uAEEjNa5d7av","outputId":"b64d51bc-f696-4e5a-a43a-98622b68a654"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Augmented model loaded!\n","[test] Found 40 images | Augmentation: False | Corruption: None\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [clean]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:54<00:00,  5.49s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Clean mIoU: 0.4775\n","[test] Found 40 images | Augmentation: False | Corruption: fog\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [fog]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:20<00:00,  2.02s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["fog                  mIoU: 0.4646 | Gap: 0.0129\n","[test] Found 40 images | Augmentation: False | Corruption: gaussian_noise\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [gaussian_noise]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:54<00:00,  5.49s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["gaussian_noise       mIoU: 0.4611 | Gap: 0.0164\n","[test] Found 40 images | Augmentation: False | Corruption: blur\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [blur]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:11<00:00,  1.10s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["blur                 mIoU: 0.4814 | Gap: -0.0039\n","[test] Found 40 images | Augmentation: False | Corruption: brightness\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [brightness]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:14<00:00,  1.48s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["brightness           mIoU: 0.4523 | Gap: 0.0253\n","[test] Found 40 images | Augmentation: False | Corruption: contrast\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [contrast]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:21<00:00,  2.15s/it]"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["contrast             mIoU: 0.4659 | Gap: 0.0116\n","\n","=================================================================\n","Corruption             Baseline  Augmented  Improvement\n","-----------------------------------------------------------------\n","clean                    0.4507     0.4775      +0.0268\n","fog                      0.4298     0.4646      +0.0348\n","gaussian_noise           0.4361     0.4611      +0.0250\n","blur                     0.4576     0.4814      +0.0238\n","brightness               0.4400     0.4523      +0.0123\n","contrast                 0.4393     0.4659      +0.0266\n","=================================================================\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["\n"]}],"source":["# ── Load Augmented Model ────────────────────────────────────────\n","model_aug = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name    = \"efficientnet-b0\",\n","    encoder_weights = None,\n","    in_channels     = 3,\n","    classes         = NUM_CLASSES,\n",").to(device)\n","\n","model_aug.load_state_dict(torch.load(CHECKPOINT_AUG, map_location=device))\n","model_aug.eval()\n","print(\"Augmented model loaded!\")\n","\n","# ── Evaluate Function ───────────────────────────────────────────\n","def evaluate(model, corruption=None):\n","    ds = VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"test\", IMAGE_SIZE, corruption=corruption)\n","    dl = DataLoader(ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n","    scores = []\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for images, masks in tqdm(dl, desc=f\"Testing [{corruption or 'clean'}]\"):\n","            images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","            preds = torch.argmax(model(images), dim=1)\n","            scores.append(compute_miou(preds, masks))\n","    return np.mean(scores)\n","\n","# ── Run All Evaluations ─────────────────────────────────────────\n","results_aug = {}\n","results_aug[\"clean\"] = evaluate(model_aug, corruption=None)\n","print(f\"Clean mIoU: {results_aug['clean']:.4f}\")\n","\n","for corruption in CORRUPTIONS.keys():\n","    results_aug[corruption] = evaluate(model_aug, corruption=corruption)\n","    gap = results_aug[\"clean\"] - results_aug[corruption]\n","    print(f\"{corruption:20s} mIoU: {results_aug[corruption]:.4f} | Gap: {gap:.4f}\")\n","\n","# ── Final Comparison Table ──────────────────────────────────────\n","baseline = {\"clean\": 0.4507, \"fog\": 0.4298, \"gaussian_noise\": 0.4361,\n","            \"blur\": 0.4576, \"brightness\": 0.4400, \"contrast\": 0.4393}\n","\n","print(f\"\\n{'='*65}\")\n","print(f\"{'Corruption':<20} {'Baseline':>10} {'Augmented':>10} {'Improvement':>12}\")\n","print(\"-\" * 65)\n","for k, v in results_aug.items():\n","    base = baseline[k]\n","    imp  = v - base\n","    print(f\"{k:<20} {base:>10.4f} {v:>10.4f} {imp:>+12.4f}\")\n","print(f\"{'='*65}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"background_save":true,"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","output_embedded_package_id":"1KRYWbiBv6LslMqqTjjc8SISpKngCMGPi"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":23063,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777558470671,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"0BD4EtplsQ9Y","outputId":"7ba3915c-0099-44bb-920f-6fc74fa50909"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Output hidden; open in https://colab.research.google.com to view."},"metadata":{}}],"source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import matplotlib.patches as mpatches\n","\n","# Class colors for VDD dataset\n","CLASS_COLORS = {\n","    0: ([128, 0, 0],   \"Wall\"),\n","    1: ([128, 128, 0], \"Roof\"),\n","    2: ([128, 64, 128],\"Road\"),\n","    3: ([0, 0, 192],   \"Water\"),\n","    4: ([64, 0, 128],  \"Vehicle\"),\n","    5: ([0, 128, 0],   \"Vegetation\"),\n","    6: ([0, 0, 0],     \"Others\"),\n","}\n","\n","def mask_to_color(mask):\n","    h, w = mask.shape\n","    color_mask = np.zeros((h, w, 3), dtype=np.uint8)\n","    for cls, (color, _) in CLASS_COLORS.items():\n","        color_mask[mask == cls] = color\n","    return color_mask\n","\n","# Load both models\n","model_clean = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name=\"efficientnet-b0\",\n","    encoder_weights=None,\n","    in_channels=3,\n","    classes=NUM_CLASSES,\n",").to(device)\n","model_clean.load_state_dict(torch.load(CHECKPOINT, map_location=device))\n","model_clean.eval()\n","\n","model_aug = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name=\"efficientnet-b0\",\n","    encoder_weights=None,\n","    in_channels=3,\n","    classes=NUM_CLASSES,\n",").to(device)\n","model_aug.load_state_dict(torch.load(CHECKPOINT_AUG, map_location=device))\n","model_aug.eval()\n","\n","# Pick 3 test images\n","test_images = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(DATASET_PATH, \"test\", \"src\", \"*.JPG\")))[:3]\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(3, 5, figsize=(25, 15))\n","titles = [\"Original Image\", \"Ground Truth\", \"Clean Model\", \"Foggy Input\", \"Aug Model (Fog)\"]\n","\n","for row, img_path in enumerate(test_images):\n","    name      = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(img_path))[0]\n","    mask_path = os.path.join(DATASET_PATH, \"test\", \"gt\", name + \".png\")\n","\n","    # Load image and mask\n","    image = cv2.cvtColor(cv2.imread(img_path), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","    mask  = np.array(Image.open(mask_path))\n","    mask  = np.clip(mask, 0, 6)\n","\n","    # Resize\n","    image_small = cv2.resize(image, (512, 512))\n","    mask_small  = cv2.resize(mask, (512, 512), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST)\n","\n","    # Apply fog\n","    foggy_image = add_fog(image_small, severity=2)\n","\n","    # Predict with clean model\n","    inp = torch.from_numpy(image_small.astype(np.float32)/255.0).permute(2,0,1).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        pred_clean = torch.argmax(model_clean(inp), dim=1).squeeze().cpu().numpy()\n","\n","    # Predict with augmented model on foggy image\n","    inp_fog = torch.from_numpy(foggy_image.astype(np.float32)/255.0).permute(2,0,1).unsqueeze(0).to(device)\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        pred_aug = torch.argmax(model_aug(inp_fog), dim=1).squeeze().cpu().numpy()\n","\n","    # Plot\n","    axes[row, 0].imshow(image_small)\n","    axes[row, 0].set_title(titles[0])\n","    axes[row, 0].axis(\"off\")\n","\n","    axes[row, 1].imshow(mask_to_color(mask_small))\n","    axes[row, 1].set_title(titles[1])\n","    axes[row, 1].axis(\"off\")\n","\n","    axes[row, 2].imshow(mask_to_color(pred_clean))\n","    axes[row, 2].set_title(titles[2])\n","    axes[row, 2].axis(\"off\")\n","\n","    axes[row, 3].imshow(foggy_image)\n","    axes[row, 3].set_title(titles[3])\n","    axes[row, 3].axis(\"off\")\n","\n","    axes[row, 4].imshow(mask_to_color(pred_aug))\n","    axes[row, 4].set_title(titles[4])\n","    axes[row, 4].axis(\"off\")\n","\n","# Legend\n","patches = [mpatches.Patch(color=np.array(c)/255, label=n) for _, (c, n) in CLASS_COLORS.items()]\n","fig.legend(handles=patches, loc=\"lower center\", ncol=7, fontsize=12)\n","plt.suptitle(\"VDD Segmentation Results — Baseline vs Augmented Model\", fontsize=16)\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig(\"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/segmentation_maps.png\", dpi=150, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n","plt.show()\n","print(\"Saved to Google Drive!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"collapsed":true,"executionInfo":{"elapsed":9298,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777558539139,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"SRcW8VY4vV6K","outputId":"4706b71e-97e9-4f6e-c9e7-ee0843c5836b"},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x600 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Chart saved to Google Drive!\n"]}],"source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","corruptions  = [\"clean\", \"fog\", \"gaussian_noise\", \"blur\", \"brightness\", \"contrast\"]\n","baseline     = [0.4507, 0.4298, 0.4361, 0.4576, 0.4400, 0.4393]\n","augmented    = [0.4775, 0.4646, 0.4611, 0.4814, 0.4523, 0.4659]\n","\n","x     = np.arange(len(corruptions))\n","width = 0.35\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 6))\n","bars1 = ax.bar(x - width/2, baseline,  width, label=\"Baseline Model\",   color=\"#E74C3C\", alpha=0.85)\n","bars2 = ax.bar(x + width/2, augmented, width, label=\"Augmented Model\",  color=\"#2ECC71\", alpha=0.85)\n","\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"Corruption Type\",  fontsize=13)\n","ax.set_ylabel(\"mIoU Score\",       fontsize=13)\n","ax.set_title(\"Robustness Comparison — Baseline vs Augmented EfficientNet on VDD\", fontsize=14)\n","ax.set_xticks(x)\n","ax.set_xticklabels(corruptions, rotation=15, fontsize=11)\n","ax.set_ylim(0.38, 0.52)\n","ax.legend(fontsize=12)\n","ax.yaxis.grid(True, linestyle=\"--\", alpha=0.7)\n","\n","# Add value labels on bars\n","for bar in bars1:\n","    ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2, bar.get_height() + 0.002,\n","            f\"{bar.get_height():.3f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=9)\n","for bar in bars2:\n","    ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2, bar.get_height() + 0.002,\n","            f\"{bar.get_height():.3f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=9)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig(\"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/robustness_chart.png\", dpi=150, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n","plt.show()\n","print(\"Chart saved to Google Drive!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":211},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":8186,"status":"error","timestamp":1777574715664,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"Q_AGpk-qvpzo","outputId":"20a575bd-9cc2-4cfc-84f2-323e02baba27"},"outputs":[{"ename":"NameError","evalue":"name 'CORRUPTIONS' is not defined","output_type":"error","traceback":["\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m","\u001b[0;31mNameError\u001b[0m                                 Traceback (most recent call last)","\u001b[0;32m/tmp/ipykernel_4053/676440648.py\u001b[0m in \u001b[0;36m<cell line: 0>\u001b[0;34m()\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m     27\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m     28\u001b[0m \u001b[0;31m# Add to CORRUPTIONS dict\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0;32m---> 29\u001b[0;31m \u001b[0mCORRUPTIONS\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m[\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\"rain\"\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m]\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m \u001b[0madd_rain\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m     30\u001b[0m \u001b[0mCORRUPTIONS\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m[\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\"snow\"\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m]\u001b[0m \u001b[0;34m=\u001b[0m \u001b[0madd_snow\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m     31\u001b[0m \u001b[0mprint\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\"Rain and Snow corruptions added!\"\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0;31mNameError\u001b[0m: name 'CORRUPTIONS' is not defined"]}],"source":["import time\n","import torch\n","# ── Add Rain and Snow corruptions ──────────────────────────────\n","def add_rain(image, severity=2):\n","    num_drops = [500, 1000, 1500, 2000, 2500][severity - 1]\n","    img = image.copy()\n","    h, w = img.shape[:2]\n","    for _ in range(num_drops):\n","        x1 = np.random.randint(0, w)\n","        y1 = np.random.randint(0, h)\n","        x2 = x1 + np.random.randint(1, 8)\n","        y2 = y1 + np.random.randint(5, 15)\n","        x2, y2 = min(x2, w-1), min(y2, h-1)\n","        cv2.line(img, (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (200, 200, 220), 1)\n","    return img\n","\n","def add_snow(image, severity=2):\n","    num_flakes = [300, 600, 900, 1200, 1500][severity - 1]\n","    img = image.copy().astype(np.float32)\n","    h, w = img.shape[:2]\n","    for _ in range(num_flakes):\n","        x = np.random.randint(0, w)\n","        y = np.random.randint(0, h)\n","        r = np.random.randint(1, 3)\n","        cv2.circle(img, (x, y), r, (240, 240, 255), -1)\n","    return np.clip(img, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","# Add to CORRUPTIONS dict\n","CORRUPTIONS[\"rain\"] = add_rain\n","CORRUPTIONS[\"snow\"] = add_snow\n","print(\"Rain and Snow corruptions added!\")\n","\n","# ── F1-score metric ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n","def compute_f1(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds  = preds.cpu().numpy()\n","    labels = labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    f1_list = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        tp = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        fp = ((preds == cls) & (labels != cls)).sum()\n","        fn = ((preds != cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if (tp + fp + fn) == 0:\n","            continue\n","        precision = tp / (tp + fp + 1e-8)\n","        recall    = tp / (tp + fn + 1e-8)\n","        f1 = 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall + 1e-8)\n","        f1_list.append(f1)\n","    return np.mean(f1_list) if f1_list else 0.0\n","\n","print(\"F1-score metric defined!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":383},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":118,"status":"error","timestamp":1777574778023,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"FktIUWI1tU9J","outputId":"1d65e15d-d643-40fe-f9f1-ae4e04648d1a"},"outputs":[{"ename":"ModuleNotFoundError","evalue":"No module named 'segmentation_models_pytorch'","output_type":"error","traceback":["\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m","\u001b[0;31mModuleNotFoundError\u001b[0m                       Traceback (most recent call last)","\u001b[0;32m/tmp/ipykernel_4053/815979242.py\u001b[0m in \u001b[0;36m<cell line: 0>\u001b[0;34m()\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m      3\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32mfrom\u001b[0m \u001b[0mPIL\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32mimport\u001b[0m \u001b[0mImage\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m      4\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32mfrom\u001b[0m \u001b[0mtqdm\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32mimport\u001b[0m \u001b[0mtqdm\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0;32m----> 5\u001b[0;31m \u001b[0;32mimport\u001b[0m \u001b[0msegmentation_models_pytorch\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32mas\u001b[0m \u001b[0msmp\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[0m\u001b[1;32m      6\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32mfrom\u001b[0m \u001b[0mgoogle\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m.\u001b[0m\u001b[0mcolab\u001b[0m \u001b[0;32mimport\u001b[0m \u001b[0mdrive\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n\u001b[1;32m      7\u001b[0m \u001b[0mdrive\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m.\u001b[0m\u001b[0mmount\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m(\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m'/gdrive'\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m)\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0;34m\u001b[0m\u001b[0m\n","\u001b[0;31mModuleNotFoundError\u001b[0m: No module named 'segmentation_models_pytorch'","","\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0;32m\nNOTE: If your import is failing due to a missing package, you can\nmanually install dependencies using either !pip or !apt.\n\nTo view examples of installing some common dependencies, click the\n\"Open Examples\" button below.\n\u001b[0;31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[0m\n"]}],"source":["import os, numpy as np, torch, torch.nn as nn, cv2, glob\n","from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n","from PIL import Image\n","from tqdm import tqdm\n","import segmentation_models_pytorch as smp\n","from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/gdrive')\n","\n","DATASET_PATH   = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"\n","IMAGE_SIZE     = 512\n","BATCH_SIZE     = 4\n","NUM_CLASSES    = 7\n","CHECKPOINT     = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_clean_best.pth\"\n","CHECKPOINT_AUG = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_augmented_best.pth\"\n","\n","def add_fog(image, severity=2):\n","    fog_intensity = [0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.85, 0.95][severity - 1]\n","    fog_layer = np.ones_like(image, dtype=np.float32) * 255\n","    result = image.astype(np.float32) * (1 - fog_intensity) + fog_layer * fog_intensity\n","    return np.clip(result, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_gaussian_noise(image, severity=2):\n","    std = [0.04, 0.06, 0.09, 0.17, 0.26][severity - 1] * 255\n","    noise = np.random.normal(0, std, image.shape).astype(np.float32)\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) + noise, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_blur(image, severity=2):\n","    k = [3, 5, 7, 9, 11][severity - 1]\n","    return cv2.GaussianBlur(image, (k, k), 0)\n","\n","def reduce_brightness(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.45, 0.3, 0.15][severity - 1]\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) * factor, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def reduce_contrast(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2, 0.1][severity - 1]\n","    mean = np.mean(image)\n","    return np.clip((image.astype(np.float32) - mean) * factor + mean, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_rain(image, severity=2):\n","    num_drops = [500, 1000, 1500, 2000, 2500][severity - 1]\n","    img = image.copy()\n","    h, w = img.shape[:2]\n","    for _ in range(num_drops):\n","        x1 = np.random.randint(0, w)\n","        y1 = np.random.randint(0, h)\n","        x2 = x1 + np.random.randint(1, 8)\n","        y2 = y1 + np.random.randint(5, 15)\n","        x2, y2 = min(x2, w-1), min(y2, h-1)\n","        cv2.line(img, (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (200, 200, 220), 1)\n","    return img\n","\n","def add_snow(image, severity=2):\n","    num_flakes = [300, 600, 900, 1200, 1500][severity - 1]\n","    img = image.copy().astype(np.float32)\n","    h, w = img.shape[:2]\n","    for _ in range(num_flakes):\n","        x = np.random.randint(0, w)\n","        y = np.random.randint(0, h)\n","        r = np.random.randint(1, 3)\n","        cv2.circle(img, (x, y), r, (240, 240, 255), -1)\n","    return np.clip(img, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","CORRUPTIONS = {\n","    \"fog\": add_fog,\n","    \"rain\": add_rain,\n","    \"snow\": add_snow,\n","    \"gaussian_noise\": add_gaussian_noise,\n","    \"blur\": add_blur,\n","    \"brightness\": reduce_brightness,\n","    \"contrast\": reduce_contrast,\n","}\n","\n","class VDDDataset(Dataset):\n","    def __init__(self, dataset_path, split=\"test\", image_size=512, augmentation=False, corruption=None, severity=2):\n","        self.image_size   = image_size\n","        self.augmentation = augmentation\n","        self.corruption   = corruption\n","        self.severity     = severity\n","        self.image_dir    = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","        self.mask_dir     = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","        self.images       = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(self.image_dir, \"*.JPG\")))\n","        print(f\"[{split}] Found {len(self.images)} images\")\n","\n","    def __len__(self):\n","        return len(self.images)\n","\n","    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n","        img_path  = self.images[idx]\n","        name      = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(img_path))[0]\n","        mask_path = os.path.join(self.mask_dir, name + \".png\")\n","        image = cv2.cvtColor(cv2.imread(img_path), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","        mask  = np.array(Image.open(mask_path))\n","        if self.augmentation:\n","            corruption = np.random.choice(list(CORRUPTIONS.keys()))\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[corruption](image, severity=np.random.randint(1, 4))\n","        if self.corruption:\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[self.corruption](image, self.severity)\n","        image = cv2.resize(image, (self.image_size, self.image_size))\n","        mask  = cv2.resize(mask, (self.image_size, self.image_size), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST)\n","        mask  = np.clip(mask, 0, 6)\n","        image = torch.from_numpy(image.astype(np.float32) / 255.0).permute(2, 0, 1)\n","        mask  = torch.from_numpy(mask).long()\n","        return image, mask\n","\n","def compute_miou(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds, labels = preds.cpu().numpy(), labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    ious = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        inter = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        union = ((preds == cls) | (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if union > 0:\n","            ious.append(inter / union)\n","    return np.mean(ious) if ious else 0.0\n","\n","def compute_f1(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds  = preds.cpu().numpy()\n","    labels = labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    f1_list = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        tp = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        fp = ((preds == cls) & (labels != cls)).sum()\n","        fn = ((preds != cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if (tp + fp + fn) == 0:\n","            continue\n","        precision = tp / (tp + fp + 1e-8)\n","        recall    = tp / (tp + fn + 1e-8)\n","        f1 = 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall + 1e-8)\n","        f1_list.append(f1)\n","    return np.mean(f1_list) if f1_list else 0.0\n","\n","device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n","print(f\"Using device: {device}\")\n","print(\"All setup complete!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"8mbS8NuetpLg"},"outputs":[],"source":["!pip install segmentation-models-pytorch -q\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":33649,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777574905725,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"TTmwdxh2txE1","outputId":"6256f354-d369-448d-b4f9-34bd1176ca10"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Mounted at /gdrive\n","Using device: cuda\n","All setup complete!\n"]}],"source":["import os, numpy as np, torch, torch.nn as nn, cv2, glob\n","from torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\n","from PIL import Image\n","from tqdm import tqdm\n","import segmentation_models_pytorch as smp\n","from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/gdrive')\n","\n","DATASET_PATH   = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/VDD/VDD\"\n","IMAGE_SIZE     = 512\n","BATCH_SIZE     = 4\n","NUM_CLASSES    = 7\n","CHECKPOINT     = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_clean_best.pth\"\n","CHECKPOINT_AUG = \"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/efficientnet_augmented_best.pth\"\n","\n","def add_fog(image, severity=2):\n","    fog_intensity = [0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.85, 0.95][severity - 1]\n","    fog_layer = np.ones_like(image, dtype=np.float32) * 255\n","    result = image.astype(np.float32) * (1 - fog_intensity) + fog_layer * fog_intensity\n","    return np.clip(result, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_gaussian_noise(image, severity=2):\n","    std = [0.04, 0.06, 0.09, 0.17, 0.26][severity - 1] * 255\n","    noise = np.random.normal(0, std, image.shape).astype(np.float32)\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) + noise, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_blur(image, severity=2):\n","    k = [3, 5, 7, 9, 11][severity - 1]\n","    return cv2.GaussianBlur(image, (k, k), 0)\n","\n","def reduce_brightness(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.45, 0.3, 0.15][severity - 1]\n","    return np.clip(image.astype(np.float32) * factor, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def reduce_contrast(image, severity=2):\n","    factor = [0.8, 0.6, 0.4, 0.2, 0.1][severity - 1]\n","    mean = np.mean(image)\n","    return np.clip((image.astype(np.float32) - mean) * factor + mean, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","def add_rain(image, severity=2):\n","    num_drops = [500, 1000, 1500, 2000, 2500][severity - 1]\n","    img = image.copy()\n","    h, w = img.shape[:2]\n","    for _ in range(num_drops):\n","        x1 = np.random.randint(0, w)\n","        y1 = np.random.randint(0, h)\n","        x2 = x1 + np.random.randint(1, 8)\n","        y2 = y1 + np.random.randint(5, 15)\n","        x2, y2 = min(x2, w-1), min(y2, h-1)\n","        cv2.line(img, (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (200, 200, 220), 1)\n","    return img\n","\n","def add_snow(image, severity=2):\n","    num_flakes = [300, 600, 900, 1200, 1500][severity - 1]\n","    img = image.copy().astype(np.float32)\n","    h, w = img.shape[:2]\n","    for _ in range(num_flakes):\n","        x = np.random.randint(0, w)\n","        y = np.random.randint(0, h)\n","        r = np.random.randint(1, 3)\n","        cv2.circle(img, (x, y), r, (240, 240, 255), -1)\n","    return np.clip(img, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","CORRUPTIONS = {\n","    \"fog\": add_fog,\n","    \"rain\": add_rain,\n","    \"snow\": add_snow,\n","    \"gaussian_noise\": add_gaussian_noise,\n","    \"blur\": add_blur,\n","    \"brightness\": reduce_brightness,\n","    \"contrast\": reduce_contrast,\n","}\n","\n","class VDDDataset(Dataset):\n","    def __init__(self, dataset_path, split=\"test\", image_size=512, augmentation=False, corruption=None, severity=2):\n","        self.image_size   = image_size\n","        self.augmentation = augmentation\n","        self.corruption   = corruption\n","        self.severity     = severity\n","        self.image_dir    = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"src\")\n","        self.mask_dir     = os.path.join(dataset_path, split, \"gt\")\n","        self.images       = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(self.image_dir, \"*.JPG\")))\n","        print(f\"[{split}] Found {len(self.images)} images\")\n","\n","    def __len__(self):\n","        return len(self.images)\n","\n","    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n","        img_path  = self.images[idx]\n","        name      = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(img_path))[0]\n","        mask_path = os.path.join(self.mask_dir, name + \".png\")\n","        image = cv2.cvtColor(cv2.imread(img_path), cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n","        mask  = np.array(Image.open(mask_path))\n","        if self.augmentation:\n","            corruption = np.random.choice(list(CORRUPTIONS.keys()))\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[corruption](image, severity=np.random.randint(1, 4))\n","        if self.corruption:\n","            image = CORRUPTIONS[self.corruption](image, self.severity)\n","        image = cv2.resize(image, (self.image_size, self.image_size))\n","        mask  = cv2.resize(mask, (self.image_size, self.image_size), interpolation=cv2.INTER_NEAREST)\n","        mask  = np.clip(mask, 0, 6)\n","        image = torch.from_numpy(image.astype(np.float32) / 255.0).permute(2, 0, 1)\n","        mask  = torch.from_numpy(mask).long()\n","        return image, mask\n","\n","def compute_miou(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds, labels = preds.cpu().numpy(), labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    ious = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        inter = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        union = ((preds == cls) | (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if union > 0:\n","            ious.append(inter / union)\n","    return np.mean(ious) if ious else 0.0\n","\n","def compute_f1(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds  = preds.cpu().numpy()\n","    labels = labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    f1_list = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        tp = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        fp = ((preds == cls) & (labels != cls)).sum()\n","        fn = ((preds != cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if (tp + fp + fn) == 0:\n","            continue\n","        precision = tp / (tp + fp + 1e-8)\n","        recall    = tp / (tp + fn + 1e-8)\n","        f1 = 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall + 1e-8)\n","        f1_list.append(f1)\n","    return np.mean(f1_list) if f1_list else 0.0\n","\n","device = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n","print(f\"Using device: {device}\")\n","print(\"All setup complete!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"elapsed":120,"status":"ok","timestamp":1777574926091,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"},"user_tz":-180},"id":"OgiB9hQnuADC","outputId":"7132389e-e751-4748-cf33-eda3f1f00002"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Rain and Snow corruptions added!\n","F1-score metric defined!\n"]}],"source":["import time\n","import torch\n","# ── Add Rain and Snow corruptions ──────────────────────────────\n","def add_rain(image, severity=2):\n","    num_drops = [500, 1000, 1500, 2000, 2500][severity - 1]\n","    img = image.copy()\n","    h, w = img.shape[:2]\n","    for _ in range(num_drops):\n","        x1 = np.random.randint(0, w)\n","        y1 = np.random.randint(0, h)\n","        x2 = x1 + np.random.randint(1, 8)\n","        y2 = y1 + np.random.randint(5, 15)\n","        x2, y2 = min(x2, w-1), min(y2, h-1)\n","        cv2.line(img, (x1, y1), (x2, y2), (200, 200, 220), 1)\n","    return img\n","\n","def add_snow(image, severity=2):\n","    num_flakes = [300, 600, 900, 1200, 1500][severity - 1]\n","    img = image.copy().astype(np.float32)\n","    h, w = img.shape[:2]\n","    for _ in range(num_flakes):\n","        x = np.random.randint(0, w)\n","        y = np.random.randint(0, h)\n","        r = np.random.randint(1, 3)\n","        cv2.circle(img, (x, y), r, (240, 240, 255), -1)\n","    return np.clip(img, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8)\n","\n","# Add to CORRUPTIONS dict\n","CORRUPTIONS[\"rain\"] = add_rain\n","CORRUPTIONS[\"snow\"] = add_snow\n","print(\"Rain and Snow corruptions added!\")\n","\n","# ── F1-score metric ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n","def compute_f1(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds  = preds.cpu().numpy()\n","    labels = labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    f1_list = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        tp = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        fp = ((preds == cls) & (labels != cls)).sum()\n","        fn = ((preds != cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        if (tp + fp + fn) == 0:\n","            continue\n","        precision = tp / (tp + fp + 1e-8)\n","        recall    = tp / (tp + fn + 1e-8)\n","        f1 = 2 * precision * recall / (precision + recall + 1e-8)\n","        f1_list.append(f1)\n","    return np.mean(f1_list) if f1_list else 0.0\n","\n","print(\"F1-score metric defined!\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"colab":{"background_save":true,"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"IBNTp09KuNHU","outputId":"94239960-6901-4435-e3c2-6d94319e9907"},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Both models loaded!\n","\n","--- BASELINE MODEL ---\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [clean]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:47<00:00,  4.71s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["clean                mIoU: 0.4507 | F1: 0.5508\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [fog]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:22<00:00,  2.22s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["fog                  mIoU: 0.4298 | F1: 0.5307\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [rain]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:08<00:00,  1.23it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["rain                 mIoU: 0.4501 | F1: 0.5501\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [snow]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:13<00:00,  1.36s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["snow                 mIoU: 0.4501 | F1: 0.5506\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [gaussian_noise]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:52<00:00,  5.21s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["gaussian_noise       mIoU: 0.4349 | F1: 0.5371\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [blur]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:09<00:00,  1.05it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["blur                 mIoU: 0.4576 | F1: 0.5592\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [brightness]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:14<00:00,  1.41s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["brightness           mIoU: 0.4400 | F1: 0.5401\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [contrast]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:22<00:00,  2.27s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["contrast             mIoU: 0.4393 | F1: 0.5386\n","\n","--- AUGMENTED MODEL ---\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [clean]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:08<00:00,  1.11it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["clean                mIoU: 0.4775 | F1: 0.5897\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [fog]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:20<00:00,  2.02s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["fog                  mIoU: 0.4646 | F1: 0.5741\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [rain]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:09<00:00,  1.09it/s]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["rain                 mIoU: 0.4766 | F1: 0.5887\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [snow]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:12<00:00,  1.26s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["snow                 mIoU: 0.4757 | F1: 0.5880\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [gaussian_noise]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:51<00:00,  5.13s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["gaussian_noise       mIoU: 0.4617 | F1: 0.5738\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [blur]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:10<00:00,  1.03s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["blur                 mIoU: 0.4814 | F1: 0.5931\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [brightness]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:14<00:00,  1.44s/it]\n"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["brightness           mIoU: 0.4523 | F1: 0.5585\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["Testing [contrast]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:20<00:00,  2.06s/it]"]},{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["contrast             mIoU: 0.4659 | F1: 0.5743\n","\n","===========================================================================\n","Corruption            Base mIoU  Base F1   Aug mIoU   Aug F1   Improv\n","---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n","clean                    0.4507   0.5508     0.4775   0.5897  +0.0268\n","fog                      0.4298   0.5307     0.4646   0.5741  +0.0348\n","rain                     0.4501   0.5501     0.4766   0.5887  +0.0265\n","snow                     0.4501   0.5506     0.4757   0.5880  +0.0256\n","gaussian_noise           0.4349   0.5371     0.4617   0.5738  +0.0268\n","blur                     0.4576   0.5592     0.4814   0.5931  +0.0238\n","brightness               0.4400   0.5401     0.4523   0.5585  +0.0123\n","contrast                 0.4393   0.5386     0.4659   0.5743  +0.0267\n","===========================================================================\n"]},{"name":"stderr","output_type":"stream","text":["\n"]}],"source":["# ── Updated evaluate function with F1 ──────────────────────────\n","def evaluate_full(model, corruption=None):\n","    ds = VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"test\", IMAGE_SIZE, corruption=corruption)\n","    dl = DataLoader(ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n","    miou_scores, f1_scores = [], []\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for images, masks in tqdm(dl, desc=f\"Testing [{corruption or 'clean'}]\"):\n","            images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","            preds = torch.argmax(model(images), dim=1)\n","            miou_scores.append(compute_miou(preds, masks))\n","            f1_scores.append(compute_f1(preds, masks))\n","    return np.mean(miou_scores), np.mean(f1_scores)\n","\n","# ── Load both models ────────────────────────────────────────────\n","model_clean = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name=\"efficientnet-b0\", encoder_weights=None,\n","    in_channels=3, classes=NUM_CLASSES).to(device)\n","model_clean.load_state_dict(torch.load(CHECKPOINT, map_location=device))\n","model_clean.eval()\n","\n","model_aug = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name=\"efficientnet-b0\", encoder_weights=None,\n","    in_channels=3, classes=NUM_CLASSES).to(device)\n","model_aug.load_state_dict(torch.load(CHECKPOINT_AUG, map_location=device))\n","model_aug.eval()\n","\n","print(\"Both models loaded!\")\n","\n","# ── Run full evaluation ─────────────────────────────────────────\n","corruptions_list = [\"fog\", \"rain\", \"snow\", \"gaussian_noise\",\n","                    \"blur\", \"brightness\", \"contrast\"]\n","\n","print(\"\\n--- BASELINE MODEL ---\")\n","results_clean = {}\n","miou, f1 = evaluate_full(model_clean, None)\n","results_clean[\"clean\"] = (miou, f1)\n","print(f\"{'clean':20s} mIoU: {miou:.4f} | F1: {f1:.4f}\")\n","for c in corruptions_list:\n","    miou, f1 = evaluate_full(model_clean, c)\n","    results_clean[c] = (miou, f1)\n","    print(f\"{c:20s} mIoU: {miou:.4f} | F1: {f1:.4f}\")\n","\n","print(\"\\n--- AUGMENTED MODEL ---\")\n","results_aug = {}\n","miou, f1 = evaluate_full(model_aug, None)\n","results_aug[\"clean\"] = (miou, f1)\n","print(f\"{'clean':20s} mIoU: {miou:.4f} | F1: {f1:.4f}\")\n","for c in corruptions_list:\n","    miou, f1 = evaluate_full(model_aug, c)\n","    results_aug[c] = (miou, f1)\n","    print(f\"{c:20s} mIoU: {miou:.4f} | F1: {f1:.4f}\")\n","\n","# ── Summary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(f\"\\n{'='*75}\")\n","print(f\"{'Corruption':<20} {'Base mIoU':>10} {'Base F1':>8} {'Aug mIoU':>10} {'Aug F1':>8} {'Improv':>8}\")\n","print(\"-\" * 75)\n","for k in [\"clean\"] + corruptions_list:\n","    bm, bf = results_clean[k]\n","    am, af = results_aug[k]\n","    imp = am - bm\n","    print(f\"{k:<20} {bm:>10.4f} {bf:>8.4f} {am:>10.4f} {af:>8.4f} {imp:>+8.4f}\")\n","print(f\"{'='*75}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"sIPN7yRNuRtm","colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1777577001177,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":7490,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"}},"outputId":"9f2b2107-1f22-47b5-d8a2-1c77f16bb69f"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["FPS:              70.72 frames/second\n","Inference time:   14.14 ms per image\n","GPU Memory usage: 132.85 MB\n","FLOPs:            2.38 GFLOPs\n","Parameters:       0.94 M\n","\n","=============================================\n","EFFICIENCY SUMMARY — EfficientNet-b0\n","=============================================\n","FPS (T4 GPU):     70.72 frames/sec\n","Latency:          14.14 ms/image\n","GPU Memory:       132.85 MB\n","GFLOPs:           2.38\n","Parameters:       0.94 M\n","=============================================\n"]}],"source":["import time\n","import torch\n","\n","# ── Load model ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","model_clean = smp.DeepLabV3Plus(\n","    encoder_name=\"efficientnet-b0\", encoder_weights=None,\n","    in_channels=3, classes=NUM_CLASSES).to(device)\n","model_clean.load_state_dict(torch.load(CHECKPOINT, map_location=device))\n","model_clean.eval()\n","\n","# ── FPS Measurement ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n","dummy_input = torch.randn(1, 3, 512, 512).to(device)\n","\n","# Warmup\n","with torch.no_grad():\n","    for _ in range(10):\n","        _ = model_clean(dummy_input)\n","\n","# Measure\n","num_runs = 50\n","torch.cuda.synchronize()\n","start = time.time()\n","with torch.no_grad():\n","    for _ in range(num_runs):\n","        _ = model_clean(dummy_input)\n","torch.cuda.synchronize()\n","end = time.time()\n","\n","fps = num_runs / (end - start)\n","ms_per_image = (end - start) / num_runs * 1000\n","print(f\"FPS:              {fps:.2f} frames/second\")\n","print(f\"Inference time:   {ms_per_image:.2f} ms per image\")\n","\n","# ── GPU Memory ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","torch.cuda.reset_peak_memory_stats()\n","with torch.no_grad():\n","    _ = model_clean(dummy_input)\n","torch.cuda.synchronize()\n","\n","memory_mb = torch.cuda.max_memory_allocated() / 1024 / 1024\n","print(f\"GPU Memory usage: {memory_mb:.2f} MB\")\n","\n","# ── FLOPs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","!pip install thop -q\n","from thop import profile\n","\n","with torch.no_grad():\n","    flops, params = profile(model_clean, inputs=(dummy_input,), verbose=False)\n","\n","gflops = flops / 1e9\n","mparams = params / 1e6\n","print(f\"FLOPs:            {gflops:.2f} GFLOPs\")\n","print(f\"Parameters:       {mparams:.2f} M\")\n","\n","# ── Summary ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(f\"\\n{'='*45}\")\n","print(f\"EFFICIENCY SUMMARY — EfficientNet-b0\")\n","print(f\"{'='*45}\")\n","print(f\"FPS (T4 GPU):     {fps:.2f} frames/sec\")\n","print(f\"Latency:          {ms_per_image:.2f} ms/image\")\n","print(f\"GPU Memory:       {memory_mb:.2f} MB\")\n","print(f\"GFLOPs:           {gflops:.2f}\")\n","print(f\"Parameters:       {mparams:.2f} M\")\n","print(f\"{'='*45}\")"]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["CLASS_NAMES = [\"Wall\", \"Roof\", \"Road\", \"Water\", \"Vehicle\", \"Vegetation\", \"Others\"]\n","\n","def compute_per_class_miou(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds  = preds.cpu().numpy()\n","    labels = labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    ious = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        inter = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        union = ((preds == cls) | (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        ious.append(inter / union if union > 0 else None)\n","    return ious\n","\n","def evaluate_per_class(model, corruption=None):\n","    ds = VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"test\", IMAGE_SIZE, corruption=corruption)\n","    dl = DataLoader(ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n","    all_ious = [[] for _ in range(NUM_CLASSES)]\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for images, masks in tqdm(dl, desc=f\"[{corruption or 'clean'}]\"):\n","            images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","            preds = torch.argmax(model(images), dim=1)\n","            batch_ious = compute_per_class_miou(preds, masks)\n","            for cls in range(NUM_CLASSES):\n","                if batch_ious[cls] is not None:\n","                    all_ious[cls].append(batch_ious[cls])\n","    return [np.mean(ious) if ious else 0.0 for ious in all_ious]\n","\n","# ── Evaluate both models on clean data ─────────────────────────\n","print(\"Evaluating baseline model per class...\")\n","clean_ious  = evaluate_per_class(model_clean, corruption=None)\n","\n","print(\"Evaluating augmented model per class...\")\n","aug_ious    = evaluate_per_class(model_aug, corruption=None)\n","\n","# ── Print table ─────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(f\"\\n{'='*55}\")\n","print(f\"{'Class':<15} {'Baseline mIoU':>14} {'Augmented mIoU':>15} {'Improvement':>12}\")\n","print(\"-\" * 55)\n","for i, cls in enumerate(CLASS_NAMES):\n","    imp = aug_ious[i] - clean_ious[i]\n","    print(f\"{cls:<15} {clean_ious[i]:>14.4f} {aug_ious[i]:>15.4f} {imp:>+12.4f}\")\n","print(f\"{'='*55}\")\n","\n","# ── Bar chart ───────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","x     = np.arange(len(CLASS_NAMES))\n","width = 0.35\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(13, 6))\n","bars1 = ax.bar(x - width/2, clean_ious, width, label='Baseline', color='#E74C3C', alpha=0.85)\n","bars2 = ax.bar(x + width/2, aug_ious,   width, label='Augmented', color='#2ECC71', alpha=0.85)\n","\n","ax.set_xlabel(\"Semantic Class\", fontsize=12)\n","ax.set_ylabel(\"mIoU Score\", fontsize=12)\n","ax.set_title(\"Per-Class mIoU — Baseline vs Augmented EfficientNet on VDD\", fontsize=14)\n","ax.set_xticks(x)\n","ax.set_xticklabels(CLASS_NAMES, rotation=15, fontsize=11)\n","ax.set_ylim(0, 0.8)\n","ax.legend(fontsize=12)\n","ax.yaxis.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.6)\n","\n","for bar in bars1:\n","    ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2, bar.get_height() + 0.01,\n","            f\"{bar.get_height():.3f}\", ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=8)\n","for bar in bars2:\n","    ax.text(bar.get_x() + bar.get_width()/2, bar.get_height() + 0.01,\n","            f\"{bar.get_height():.3f}\", ha='center', va='bottom', fontsize=8)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig(\"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/per_class_miou.png\", dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\n","plt.show()\n","print(\"Per-class chart saved to Google Drive!\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":937},"id":"zYgbEScz2GCn","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1777577096995,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":19595,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"}},"outputId":"afb636a9-7d0b-4b20-8728-1130302b7729"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Evaluating baseline model per class...\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["[clean]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:10<00:00,  1.05s/it]\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Evaluating augmented model per class...\n","[test] Found 40 images\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["[clean]: 100%|██████████| 10/10 [00:07<00:00,  1.32it/s]\n"]},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["\n","=======================================================\n","Class            Baseline mIoU  Augmented mIoU  Improvement\n","-------------------------------------------------------\n","Wall                    0.4601          0.4805      +0.0204\n","Roof                    0.3359          0.3876      +0.0517\n","Road                    0.5075          0.4963      -0.0112\n","Water                   0.7939          0.8005      +0.0065\n","Vehicle                 0.0003          0.1571      +0.1568\n","Vegetation              0.6522          0.6462      -0.0060\n","Others                  0.3764          0.3427      -0.0337\n","=======================================================\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1300x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Per-class chart saved to Google Drive!\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["CLASS_NAMES = [\"Wall\", \"Roof\", \"Road\", \"Water\", \"Vehicle\", \"Vegetation\", \"Others\"]\n","\n","def compute_per_class_miou(preds, labels, num_classes=7):\n","    preds  = preds.cpu().numpy()\n","    labels = labels.cpu().numpy()\n","    ious = []\n","    for cls in range(num_classes):\n","        inter = ((preds == cls) & (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        union = ((preds == cls) | (labels == cls)).sum()\n","        ious.append(inter / union if union > 0 else 0.0)\n","    return ious\n","\n","def evaluate_per_class_corruption(model, corruption=None):\n","    ds = VDDDataset(DATASET_PATH, \"test\", IMAGE_SIZE, corruption=corruption)\n","    dl = DataLoader(ds, batch_size=BATCH_SIZE, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n","    all_ious = [[] for _ in range(NUM_CLASSES)]\n","    with torch.no_grad():\n","        for images, masks in dl:\n","            images, masks = images.to(device), masks.to(device)\n","            preds = torch.argmax(model(images), dim=1)\n","            batch_ious = compute_per_class_miou(preds, masks)\n","            for cls in range(NUM_CLASSES):\n","                all_ious[cls].append(batch_ious[cls])\n","    return [np.mean(ious) for ious in all_ious]\n","\n","corruptions_list = [\"fog\", \"rain\", \"snow\", \"gaussian_noise\", \"blur\", \"brightness\", \"contrast\"]\n","\n","# ── Baseline per-class per-corruption ──────────────────────────\n","print(\"Evaluating BASELINE model per class per corruption...\")\n","baseline_perclass = {}\n","baseline_perclass[\"clean\"] = evaluate_per_class_corruption(model_clean, None)\n","print(f\"clean done\")\n","for c in corruptions_list:\n","    baseline_perclass[c] = evaluate_per_class_corruption(model_clean, c)\n","    print(f\"{c} done\")\n","\n","# ── Augmented per-class per-corruption ─────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\nEvaluating AUGMENTED model per class per corruption...\")\n","aug_perclass = {}\n","aug_perclass[\"clean\"] = evaluate_per_class_corruption(model_aug, None)\n","print(f\"clean done\")\n","for c in corruptions_list:\n","    aug_perclass[c] = evaluate_per_class_corruption(model_aug, c)\n","    print(f\"{c} done\")\n","\n","# ── Robustness Gap per class ────────────────────────────────────\n","print(f\"\\n{'='*90}\")\n","print(\"PER-CLASS ROBUSTNESS GAP — BASELINE MODEL\")\n","print(f\"{'Corruption':<20}\", end=\"\")\n","for cls in CLASS_NAMES:\n","    print(f\"{cls:>12}\", end=\"\")\n","print()\n","print(\"-\" * 90)\n","for c in corruptions_list:\n","    print(f\"{c:<20}\", end=\"\")\n","    for i in range(NUM_CLASSES):\n","        gap = baseline_perclass[\"clean\"][i] - baseline_perclass[c][i]\n","        print(f\"{gap:>+12.4f}\", end=\"\")\n","    print()\n","\n","print(f\"\\n{'='*90}\")\n","print(\"PER-CLASS ROBUSTNESS GAP — AUGMENTED MODEL\")\n","print(f\"{'Corruption':<20}\", end=\"\")\n","for cls in CLASS_NAMES:\n","    print(f\"{cls:>12}\", end=\"\")\n","print()\n","print(\"-\" * 90)\n","for c in corruptions_list:\n","    print(f\"{c:<20}\", end=\"\")\n","    for i in range(NUM_CLASSES):\n","        gap = aug_perclass[\"clean\"][i] - aug_perclass[c][i]\n","        print(f\"{gap:>+12.4f}\", end=\"\")\n","    print()\n","\n","# ── Heatmap chart ───────────────────────────────────────────────\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import numpy as np\n","\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(20, 6))\n","\n","for ax, perclass, title in zip(\n","    axes,\n","    [baseline_perclass, aug_perclass],\n","    [\"Baseline Model — Per-Class Robustness Gap\", \"Augmented Model — Per-Class Robustness Gap\"]\n","):\n","    gap_matrix = []\n","    for c in corruptions_list:\n","        row = [perclass[\"clean\"][i] - perclass[c][i] for i in range(NUM_CLASSES)]\n","        gap_matrix.append(row)\n","\n","    gap_matrix = np.array(gap_matrix)\n","    im = ax.imshow(gap_matrix, cmap=\"RdYlGn_r\", aspect=\"auto\", vmin=-0.1, vmax=0.2)\n","    ax.set_xticks(range(NUM_CLASSES))\n","    ax.set_xticklabels(CLASS_NAMES, rotation=30, fontsize=11)\n","    ax.set_yticks(range(len(corruptions_list)))\n","    ax.set_yticklabels(corruptions_list, fontsize=11)\n","    ax.set_title(title, fontsize=13, fontweight=\"bold\")\n","\n","    for i in range(len(corruptions_list)):\n","        for j in range(NUM_CLASSES):\n","            ax.text(j, i, f\"{gap_matrix[i,j]:+.3f}\",\n","                    ha=\"center\", va=\"center\", fontsize=8,\n","                    color=\"black\")\n","\n","plt.colorbar(im, ax=axes[1], label=\"Robustness Gap (positive = performance drop)\")\n","plt.suptitle(\"Per-Class Robustness Gap Heatmap — Baseline vs Augmented\", fontsize=15, fontweight=\"bold\")\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.savefig(\"/gdrive/MyDrive/VDD_project/perclass_gap_heatmap.png\", dpi=150, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n","plt.show()\n","print(\"\\nHeatmap saved to Google Drive!\")"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"xLkAPJAj2ajw","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1777577679051,"user_tz":-180,"elapsed":283373,"user":{"displayName":"WASEEM AKRAM","userId":"13176123852290996212"}},"outputId":"cc286750-4b97-4d7a-b7b7-8e3ff568a20b"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Evaluating BASELINE model per class per corruption...\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","clean done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","fog done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","rain done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","snow done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","gaussian_noise done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","blur done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","brightness done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","contrast done\n","\n","Evaluating AUGMENTED model per class per corruption...\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","clean done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","fog done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","rain done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","snow done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","gaussian_noise done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","blur done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","brightness done\n","[test] Found 40 images\n","contrast done\n","\n","==========================================================================================\n","PER-CLASS ROBUSTNESS GAP — BASELINE MODEL\n","Corruption                  Wall        Roof        Road       Water     Vehicle  Vegetation      Others\n","------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n","fog                      +0.0176     +0.0267     +0.0123     +0.0183     +0.0003     +0.0024     +0.0204\n","rain                     -0.0005     +0.0034     +0.0025     +0.0017     +0.0000     +0.0011     +0.0014\n","snow                     -0.0026     +0.0018     -0.0014     +0.0020     -0.0000     +0.0019     +0.0028\n","gaussian_noise           +0.0189     +0.0046     +0.0489     +0.0101     -0.0000     +0.0089     +0.0069\n","blur                     -0.0005     -0.0146     -0.0229     -0.0024     -0.0003     +0.0017     -0.0083\n","brightness               +0.0145     +0.0094     -0.0168     +0.0016     +0.0003     +0.0190     +0.0010\n","contrast                 +0.0108     +0.0006     +0.0036     +0.0070     +0.0003     +0.0043     +0.0076\n","\n","==========================================================================================\n","PER-CLASS ROBUSTNESS GAP — AUGMENTED MODEL\n","Corruption                  Wall        Roof        Road       Water     Vehicle  Vegetation      Others\n","------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n","fog                      +0.0065     +0.0053     +0.0012     +0.0122     +0.0459     +0.0048     +0.0119\n","rain                     +0.0013     +0.0004     -0.0003     +0.0036     +0.0008     +0.0007     -0.0001\n","snow                     +0.0012     -0.0010     +0.0001     +0.0044     +0.0010     +0.0026     +0.0038\n","gaussian_noise           +0.0156     +0.0147     +0.0431     +0.0117     +0.0196     -0.0078     +0.0200\n","blur                     +0.0010     -0.0116     -0.0073     -0.0059     +0.0053     -0.0018     -0.0072\n","brightness               +0.0134     +0.0149     +0.0008     -0.0024     +0.0598     +0.0238     +0.0005\n","contrast                 +0.0064     +0.0126     +0.0015     +0.0023     +0.0626     +0.0137     -0.0209\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 2000x600 with 3 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["\n","Heatmap saved to Google Drive!\n"]}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["!git config --global user.email \"w.akram2@studenti.unisa.it\"\n","!git config --global user.name \"wasii3336\"\n"],"metadata":{"id":"BDW4V-Ee3nKx"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["from google.colab import drive\n","drive.mount('/content/drive')"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"fVn3FUu-eEwY","executionInfo":{